{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again","id":1053873,"title":"\"Problem Players make me never want to run a game again\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-23T10:28:44-08:00","id":1053873,"title":"\"Problem Players make me never want to run a game again\"","content":"You do all this work as a ST. You provide visuals, minatures, dry erase boards, character folders, maps, background info , lend your own books etc.....and then 1-2 players decide to loot every little thing they can see for no reason , charge into every scenario in Crinos despite overwhelming odds , OOC yell and argue and talk over you , ask you follow up questions before your finished answering their initial question...goddamnit.....<br /> <br /> full disclosure, I probably smoked a pack of cigarettes in leui of jumping over the table and taking it to the streets","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T10:29:35-08:00","id":1053877,"title":"","content":"I will never ask people who play D&amp;D to join a WtA game ever , EVER, EVER again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T10:53:36-08:00","id":1053886,"title":"","content":"Sounds rough. Not sure if there is anything that can be said to help.<br /> <br /> Some groups seem to work out better or worse than others for WoD games. A while back my then gaming group (2-3 of the players) didn't really understand what the games were going for so we ended up switching over to D&amp;D for a while. Was a sad day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T10:56:06-08:00","id":1053887,"title":"","content":"This is exactly why I carefully screen everyone who may join our game. Even with that, I've had shit-shows before. No one wants to exclude people, but not every group and not every game is for everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T11:00:26-08:00","id":1053893,"title":"","content":"XD, if a player wants he can derail everything rather fast.<br /> <br /> This it's no Werewolf experience, but a ST I had once told me of a player who decided to go in a straight line to the north. Always.<br /> <br /> The ST wanted the player to go to some town or do something, but the player each time something presented in his way, any time the ST asked him What do you do?, he would always answer &quot;I advance foward&quot;.<br /> The character entered in a wood, and moved foward. Traveled trough towns and cities, foward. Faced a dragon, moved foward without caring.<br /> The player managed to get Arcadia that way. Of course, he moved foward.<br /> <br /> In a sense RP it's like a social experiment where everyone needs to agree on what they're doing. You need to be in the same page with the other players, or desist to play.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T11:02:24-08:00","id":1053894,"title":"","content":"what sucks is one of the guys is an OLD time friend of mine , but he is constantly trying to &quot;WIN&quot;. He is familiar with WtA , but still tries to pull this nonsense:<br /> <br /> Just one example for now (I know this type of thread has been done before but I gotta get this frustration out)<br /> <br /> Me: ok dude what do you wanna play<br /> Buddy: A glasswalker with 2 german shepperd attack dogs and a brand new fully loaded suburban<br /> Me: Cmon dude....really....Your a garou....why would a garou need attack dogs?! furthermore Im ok with the vehicle but where did this characters money come from<br /> Buddy: What if I just made them labradors<br /> Me: Your missing the point goddamnit<br /> Buddy: Can I have resources 4 or 5<br /> Me: You know how this goes dude this isn't your first go around , justify it and I'll let you know....How does your rank 1 character who is probably between the age of 14 - 19 have so much money<br /> Buddy: Hes an air force reservist! a computer wiz!<br /> Me: Dude.......jesus christ<br /> Buddy: How many sniper rifles can I have<br /> Me: Fuck you dude","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T11:03:51-08:00","id":1053898,"title":"","content":"You just gotta find the right group. Some people are just there to run roughshod over whatever was prepared. Keep looking for fresh meat that is interested in cooperating with you to create the story you want to tell. <br /> <br /> I played in a d20 Star Wars game for a few years, which was fun, but pretty much on the level of your average DnD game in terms of commitment and immersion (IE, not a lot). For my current WtA game I recruited the folks who I enjoyed playing with the most from that SW group, the ones who I could trust to maintain a certain level of roleplaying competency. It has worked out quite well... however, most of the people in my initial rpg group I would not have foisted a WoD game onto. Murderhobos and constant slapstick hijinks don't really compliment the flavor of the game, but often that is all people really demand of the rpg experience. You gotta find the folks that want a bit more out of their dice-rolling sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T11:08:44-08:00","id":1053901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What sucks is one of the guys is an OLD time friend of mine , but he is constantly trying to &quot;WIN&quot;. He is familiar with WtA , but still tries to pull this nonsense </div> </div> </div>That's sad.<br /> <br /> But what, exactly, does he expect of RPG?. I mean, you say he tries to win, but the things he supposedly asked for weren't terribly munchkin (except, maybe, the Resouces part).<br /> If he doesn't want to play your way...there's not much it can be done, you can't force people play your way, not even if it's &quot;the correct way&quot;. You can only hope :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T11:09:38-08:00","id":1053902,"title":"","content":"Same player different game:<br /> <br /> context: The pack of Get of Fenirs have just defeated a corrupt earth elemental (that manifested as a 4 story tall troll/giant type creature) that erupted form the ground in the middle of an isolated Shadowlord kinfolk village deep in the woods. Heres what followed:<br /> <br /> Buddy: I want to keep its bones<br /> Me: You want to keep the giants bones.....and your going to keep these &quot;giants bones&quot; where? in your hiking backpack?<br /> Buddy: Ill switch to crinos<br /> Me: Motherfucker..for real....and whats your intent with these wyrm tainted giants bones<br /> Buddy: Im going to make Glaives out of them....its a real thing look it up...not a Klaive , a Glaive!<br /> Me: You are a rank one...you don't even have tools to do such a thing...you don't even know rite of the fetish...THIS IS BARELY THE SECOND GAME DUDE!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T11:20:22-08:00","id":1053906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1053902#post1053902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same player different game:<br /> <br /> context: The pack of Get of Fenirs have just defeated a corrupt earth elemental (that manifested as a 4 story tall troll/giant type creature) that erupted form the ground in the middle of an isolated Shadowlord kinfolk village deep in the woods. Heres what followed:<br /> <br /> Buddy: I want to keep its bones<br /> Me: You want to keep the giants bones.....and your going to keep these &quot;giants bones&quot; where? in your hiking backpack?<br /> Buddy: Ill switch to crinos<br /> Me: Motherfucker..for real....and whats your intent with these wyrm tainted giants bones<br /> Buddy: Im going to make Glaives out of them....its a real thing look it up...not a Klaive , a Glaive!<br /> Me: You are a rank one...you don't even have tools to do such a thing...you don't even know rite of the fetish...THIS IS BARELY THE SECOND GAME DUDE!</div> </div> </div> </div>Did his character even have any kind of Crafts for that to even construct said polearms in the first place? It's a kind of a nitpicky question, I suppose, but I do wonder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T11:24:48-08:00","id":1053910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1053893#post1053893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">XD, if a player wants he can derail everything rather fast.<br /> <br /> This it's no Werewolf experience, but a ST I had once told me of a player who decided to go in a straight line to the north. Always.<br /> <br /> The ST wanted the player to go to some town or do something, but the player each time something presented in his way, any time the ST asked him What do you do?, he would always answer &quot;I advance foward&quot;.<br /> The character entered in a wood, and moved foward. Traveled trough towns and cities, foward. Faced a dragon, moved foward without caring.<br /> The player managed to get Arcadia that way. Of course, he moved foward.<br /> <br /> In a sense RP it's like a social experiment where everyone needs to agree on what they're doing. You need to be in the same page with the other players, or desist to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone might have played ye olde text based games, methinks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T11:25:19-08:00","id":1053911,"title":"","content":"Nope no crafts at all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T11:30:30-08:00","id":1053913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1053901#post1053901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's sad.<br /> <br /> But what, exactly, does he expect of RPG?. I mean, you say he tries to win, but the things he supposedly asked for weren't terribly munchkin (except, maybe, the Resouces part).<br /> If he doesn't want to play your way...there's not much it can be done, you can't force people play your way, not even if it's &quot;the correct way&quot;. You can only hope :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I cant cite it right off the bat , but if I remember correctly , Garou and &quot;domesticated animals&quot; don't jive.<br /> furthermore, why would a teenage kid be a high ranking RICH airforce reservist .....also how the shit would a garou be in military service?!<br /> <br /> I don't expect them to play &quot;my way&quot; but I do expect the to respect the &quot;feel&quot; of the game. When a player suggests something that I didn't think about I absolutely love it if it fits and contributes and is in line (at least SOMEWHAT) with the SPLAT and character concept.<br /> <br /> He also wanted to be a sniper with several high tech sniper rifles.....he wanted this AFTER telling me he was an air force reservist who does computer work in the military....His bullshit was coming so fast it was hard to even keep up to explain to him why it was ridiculous. I swear it felt like I was back at work dealing with at risk teenagers who don't listen , don't read, etc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T11:37:51-08:00","id":1053917,"title":"","content":"Most recent example , and the one that really made me almost blow my top:<br /> <br /> the GoF and the Corax are deep in the wilderness after defeating the corrupt earth elemental.....they come upon a dying metis Shadowlord who dies right as he is about to tell the characters what happened....the SL's last words are &quot; don't trust the....(death)&quot;.<br /> <br /> The corax who is an awesome and mature player says that he is going to eat one of the eyes to see what he can find out.....so the corax is sitting on the dead SL's chest and pecks out an eye for info. I then stated that from inside the SL's body something seems to be moving upwards as if its going to come out of the dead NPC's mouth or throat.<br /> <br /> The two GoF ( problem players) say this damn near in unison while shouting and excited at everyone at the table &quot; WE START HACKING IT WE START HACKING IT APART!&quot; (they were both in Crinos)<br /> <br /> I asked the Corax to roll dodge, and he failed....long story short...I told the GoF to roll damage then had the Corax roll soak. The problem players start congratulating each other while the corax player is looking super annoyed (this was the first 20 minutes of the session).<br /> <br /> I tell the corax about the battle scars etc..since he got caught in the crossfire of the two problem players. The two problem players then start a shit show of arguing where they say &quot; WAIT WAIT WE DIDNT WANT TO HIT THE CORAX!&quot; ...I told them they need to pay attention to the game and theirs consequences for their actions in this game (IMO). 45 minutes and 3 cigarettes later I was already at my wits end and was too frustrated to be a good ST for the rest of the session. Even the Corax player stated to the problem players &quot; You both said you were hacking at the NPC while Im sitting on its chest.....what did you expect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T12:47:37-08:00","id":1053959,"title":"","content":"It seems that there was/is a communication problem.<br /> <br /> And that your players don't respect their turn.<br /> <br /> I think you could have handwaved that the Croax just dodges without a roll, after all, it's a bogus situation, no reason to make the Croax pay for it.<br /> Usually, when player it's 'bout to do something stupid you can state something like &quot;are you sure?&quot;, or in this case, &quot;there's a guy between the target and your swords&quot;. This training wheels may be bothersome, but sometimes they pay of. <hr /><br /> Sometimes these kind of stuff hapens because the chemistry of the party isn't good. Probably the two &quot;problem players&quot; reinforce each other worse traits, even without truly wanting to. Other people may create a different chemistry, I've seen stories turn from terror to comedy just because a guy joined the table, and changed the mood despite all ST attempt to avoid it.<br /> <br /> Do whatever you can to set the mood. If the players insist in murdering your attempts, then obviously they aren't on the same page as you, and may be time to leave...after all, you want to have fun too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T12:54:00-08:00","id":1053963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1053959#post1053959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems that there was/is a communication problem.<br /> Usually, when player it's 'bout to do something stupid you can state something like &quot;are you sure?&quot;. This training wheels may be .</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I've never done . I've wanted too , but felt that it was too cheesy , but I big time see your point..I gotta view it as training wheels then ween off of saying &quot;are you sure?&quot; as the group grows in maturity. This is good advice.<br /> <br /> <br /> your right too about the communication problem and them not respecting their turn. Im just going to kick them out of the game to be honest. The other three players never have these issues and we are all on the same wavelength. I just really wanted to introduce other gamers too WtA its the only game I play and the only RPG bookline that Ive ever read since I was a kid.....not to be all foofy an shit but when they fucked up the game for me and the other players...after my anger subsided...I was super bummed and demoralized.....which I recognize is retarded because its just a game but all the same its how I felt.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12902,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","user":"WISDOMINCHAINS","date":". 02-23-2017, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T13:07:25-08:00","id":1053972,"title":"","content":"Yes, I have had my share of problem players. I try to give players warnings when they are about to do something incredibly stupid (my players tend to wince when I say the word 'interesting' or the phrase 'that is unusual' because that usually means that a character is going to die a horrible death if they do not rethink their plans). Problem players tend to learn during the first session or they leave my games after the second session because I can predict their actions after the first session and plan accordingly. Infernal Sorcerers with Mask of Innocence and a few levels of Youth, along with around 100 Soul Points worth of addition Demonic Investments, are my preferred teaching lessons for the sort of character that tends to attack everything (no matter how inappropriate) because they get that sick look on their face when they suddenly realize that they have just attacked something much, much more powerful than their characters without provocation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T17:45:43-08:00","id":1054106,"title":"","content":"I only play with gamers whose gaming style is compatible with my own. Some players I will play with in certain games, but not others because their playing style can be fine in some games for me, but not others. Some I can tolerate in one shots, but not extended campaigns.<br /> <br /> Play with those who want the same thing out of the game that you do. If they don't, don't game that with them. No matter how tempted you are to have that extra PC so you can finally play/run Game X, it never works out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T18:05:55-08:00","id":1054124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054106#post1054106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Play with those who want the same thing out of the game that you do. If they don't, don't game that with them. No matter how tempted you are to have that extra PC so you can finally play/run Game X, it never works out.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is sadly the truth more often than not.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T18:29:14-08:00","id":1054135,"title":"","content":"I had a player over a decade and a half ago.<br /> <br /> Who decided her lupus garou HAD to be an athiest since wolves dont have a religion, obviously<br /> <br /> and started to ask 'why' to every freakin thing<br /> <br /> when I said &quot;shape up or ship out'<br /> <br /> she questioned my definition of &quot; shape up&quot; <br /> <br /> she started to complain about the government not trivialy finding garou via sattelites.<br /> <br /> She called the umbra &quot;Cartoonish&quot; <br /> <br /> and the NPC she responded most favourably to, was a DNA intern, she was supposed to interrogate then kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T20:02:49-08:00","id":1054166,"title":"","content":"Yeah, wolves cannot be atheists any more than they can be brain surgeons (the level of abstraction required for atheism is far beyond the intellectual capabilities of wolves). Considering that animals can observe supernatural entities naturally according to cWoD rules, I would think that wolves would be more likely to be into animism than anything else. And I think an atheist Garou would be chucked into Erebus tail first because something is obviously wrong with her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T20:06:33-08:00","id":1054169,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of people forget that it's supposed to be Mature games for mature minds...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T21:51:09-08:00","id":1054192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054166#post1054166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, wolves cannot be atheists any more than they can be brain surgeons (the level of abstraction required for atheism is far beyond the intellectual capabilities of wolves). Considering that animals can observe supernatural entities naturally according to cWoD rules, I would think that wolves would be more likely to be into animism than anything else. And I think an atheist Garou would be chucked into Erebus tail first because something is obviously wrong with her.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there are a couple of problems with those assumptions. The first is that Lupus Garou aren't just wolves. They don't innately have less intelligence than other Garou and are capable of conceptualizing the same abstractions as other Garou, its just a matter of whether they have the experiential framework to make that conceptualization easier. The second is that you really have to define atheism more clearly. The existence of spirits and supernatural phenomena doesn't actually explicitly indicate the existence of any kind of god, nor does accepting their objective existence necessarily translate to any practice of faith. Christianity holds that the earth is God's creation. Atheists may not believe in God but that doesn't mean they stop believing that the earth exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T22:04:47-08:00","id":1054194,"title":"","content":"It depends on the atheist, I have met some that vehemently argued that nothing is real before I ran away from the lunatics. Yes, you can have spiritual atheists, but the default assumption is that people are material atheists if they do not add another qualifier. A spiritual atheist would be fine within a WtA campaign because no one is demanding the worship of specific jobs, just the willingness to do their dang job or the bravery to be a Ronin. Whining about the duties of the Garou is a good way to end up getting smacked around or even banished from the Garou Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T03:18:26-08:00","id":1054249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1053894#post1053894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what sucks is one of the guys is an OLD time friend of mine , but he is constantly trying to &amp;quot;WIN&amp;quot;. He is familiar with WtA , but still tries to pull this nonsense:<br /> <br /> Just one example for now (I know this type of thread has been done before but I gotta get this frustration out)<br /> <br /> Me: ok dude what do you wanna play<br /> Buddy: A glasswalker with 2 german shepperd attack dogs and a brand new fully loaded suburban<br /> Me: Cmon dude....really....Your a garou....why would a garou need attack dogs?! furthermore Im ok with the vehicle but where did this characters money come from<br /> Buddy: What if I just made them labradors<br /> Me: Your missing the point goddamnit<br /> Buddy: Can I have resources 4 or 5<br /> Me: You know how this goes dude this isn't your first go around , justify it and I'll let you know....How does your rank 1 character who is probably between the age of 14 - 19 have so much money<br /> Buddy: Hes an air force reservist! a computer wiz!<br /> Me: Dude.......jesus christ<br /> Buddy: How many sniper rifles can I have<br /> Me: Fuck you dude</div> </div> </div> </div>If he is a hominid, why can't he have resources 4? Maybe resources 5 would ruin your campaign (maybe even 4), but he could be the son of a rich industry Baron... Which means that his &quot;daddy&quot; won't be the typical kinfolk that Garou use as a toy... In fact, this person could use HIM as an asset. It also means he won't have an easy access to that money (daddy took my credit, I'm grounded for the entire week).<br /> He could also be some kind of infant genious. That however, is not free of charge too. He must take apropriate skills (Inteligence 5, Computer 5 or Engineering 5 or something like it) to express his &quot;own high tech company&quot; that he built with 12 years old.<br /> But that's not all: request that he also gets fame 4 or even 5. That's a curse - <u>everybody</u> knows the &quot;genius kid&quot;. Good luck trying to Crinos his way away (and if he do, send 100 fomori his way, or send several other Garou to hunt him down if he screw things up in the night news. Just kill his character if he screw things up)<br /> As for the dogs, let him have the stupid things. And make all NPCs Garou laugh out of his &quot;little lassies&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T03:30:54-08:00","id":1054250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1053902#post1053902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same player different game:<br /> <br /> context: The pack of Get of Fenirs have just defeated a corrupt earth elemental (that manifested as a 4 story tall troll/giant type creature) that erupted form the ground in the middle of an isolated Shadowlord kinfolk village deep in the woods. Heres what followed:<br /> <br /> Buddy: I want to keep its bones<br /> Me: You want to keep the giants bones.....and your going to keep these &amp;quot;giants bones&amp;quot; where? in your hiking backpack?<br /> Buddy: Ill switch to crinos<br /> Me: Motherfucker..for real....and whats your intent with these wyrm tainted giants bones<br /> Buddy: Im going to make Glaives out of them....its a real thing look it up...not a Klaive , a Glaive!<br /> Me: You are a rank one...you don't even have tools to do such a thing...you don't even know rite of the fetish...THIS IS BARELY THE SECOND GAME DUDE!</div> </div> </div> </div>Just let him have the bones, what's the problem in that? Not a giant skull the size of a car (that you can ask how he'll transport and where he will store it), but a teeth, or a finger, that would be fine. What will he do with it? As a rank 1, absolutely nothing. Or, maybe he'll find the local trinket market who use those to make alchemical potions lol. Or an Elder could be interested in those bones... Maybe the Elder could &quot;throw him a bone&quot; in exchange for a favor and the bones. Or, if you don't wanna any of that, the player can keep it as a souvenir, a trophy to show off to others","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T03:40:52-08:00","id":1054251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1053917#post1053917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most recent example , and the one that really made me almost blow my top:<br /> <br /> the GoF and the Corax are deep in the wilderness after defeating the corrupt earth elemental.....they come upon a dying metis Shadowlord who dies right as he is about to tell the characters what happened....the SL's last words are &amp;quot; don't trust the....(death)&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> The corax who is an awesome and mature player says that he is going to eat one of the eyes to see what he can find out.....so the corax is sitting on the dead SL's chest and pecks out an eye for info. I then stated that from inside the SL's body something seems to be moving upwards as if its going to come out of the dead NPC's mouth or throat.<br /> <br /> The two GoF ( problem players) say this damn near in unison while shouting and excited at everyone at the table &amp;quot; WE START HACKING IT WE START HACKING IT APART!&amp;quot; (they were both in Crinos)<br /> <br /> I asked the Corax to roll dodge, and he failed....long story short...I told the GoF to roll damage then had the Corax roll soak. The problem players start congratulating each other while the corax player is looking super annoyed (this was the first 20 minutes of the session).<br /> <br /> I tell the corax about the battle scars etc..since he got caught in the crossfire of the two problem players. The two problem players then start a shit show of arguing where they say &amp;quot; WAIT WAIT WE DIDNT WANT TO HIT THE CORAX!&amp;quot; ...I told them they need to pay attention to the game and theirs consequences for their actions in this game (IMO). 45 minutes and 3 cigarettes later I was already at my wits end and was too frustrated to be a good ST for the rest of the session. Even the Corax player stated to the problem players &amp;quot; You both said you were hacking at the NPC while Im sitting on its chest.....what did you expect</div> </div> </div> </div>But... Why would the players hit the Corax? They could've throw him away to get him out of the way, but I see no reason why they would hack the corax apart along with the dead NPC, unless they were in frenesi. Well, you could've asked before solving the scene &quot;do you just claw it away throw the Corax body?&quot;. Well, that scene doesn't make much sense to me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T08:56:00-08:00","id":1054340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054194#post1054194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on the atheist, I have met some that vehemently argued that nothing is real before I ran away from the lunatics. Yes, you can have spiritual atheists, but the default assumption is that people are material atheists if they do not add another qualifier. A spiritual atheist would be fine within a WtA campaign because no one is demanding the worship of specific jobs, just the willingness to do their dang job or the bravery to be a Ronin. Whining about the duties of the Garou is a good way to end up getting smacked around or even banished from the Garou Nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that in a world where spirits and the like actually objectively exist you can still believe in them be a material atheist, because paradoxically in such a world there's actually nothing spiritual about spirits. They're just as much part of the regular everyday world as animals and plants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T11:14:21-08:00","id":1054380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054250#post1054250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just let him have the bones, what's the problem in that? Not a giant skull the size of a car (that you can ask how he'll transport and where he will store it), but a teeth, or a finger, that would be fine. What will he do with it? As a rank 1, absolutely nothing. Or, maybe he'll find the local trinket market who use those to make alchemical potions lol. Or an Elder could be interested in those bones... Maybe the Elder could &quot;throw him a bone&quot; in exchange for a favor and the bones. Or, if you don't wanna any of that, the player can keep it as a souvenir, a trophy to show off to others</div> </div> </div> </div>If he had said that he just wanted teeth or a finger then I would have had no issue with it. And I do take some responsibility , its my game , but I have a certain expectation for players that have experience with storytelling games that you listen , think, and put yourself in the scene and your characters shoes so to speak. The problem is that this player just kept saying &quot; I want the giants bones to make weapons!&quot; I tried to probe further to help him come to the light and make a reasonable choice , but it never went that way with the player. Plus the bones were wyrm tainted , the pack was isolated in the wilderness with very very basic hiking gear and were on their way traveling twords the city. He didn't take talisman dedication , doesn't know rite of the fetish , doesn't know rite of cleansing etc......that being said....if it was a brand brand brand new player to the game I'd make allowances or introduce something to help the character out. This guy is not a new player to the game , he owns his own books....Im doubtful he reads anything except the &quot; KEWL PW3RZ!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T11:30:03-08:00","id":1054384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054251#post1054251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But... Why would the players hit the Corax? They could've throw him away to get him out of the way, but I see no reason why they would hack the corax apart along with the dead NPC, unless they were in frenesi. Well, you could've asked before solving the scene &quot;do you just claw it away throw the Corax body?&quot;. Well, that scene doesn't make much sense to me</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to preface my explanation by saying that in my personal ST code , I don't like to babysit players and hand hold them , not when they have experience with the game. Furthermore it makes me uncomfortable as a ST to step in and tell a character &quot; hey don't do that&quot; or &quot; hey do it like this&quot; because I firmly believe in consequences , especially for not paying attention. Even more deeply , through personal experience( overseas and on the streets) I know that sometimes in the heat of battle , and as a response to fear and adrenaline , you will hit your own people , and sometimes it's lethal.<br /> <br /> I say that last thing to paint this picture: A dead garou was leaning against a large tree. Characters come upon it. Instead of healing him with mothers touch , they let him die. The massive Raven hops onto the dead garou's chest and starts pecking out an eye. While he is doing his Corax thing I state that something is rumbling inside the dead garou's chest and looks like its moving upinto the dead garou's throat. I as a ST left that open for a bit to see if the Corax says &quot; Im going to fly away or hop off&quot; , no such thing was stated. I then state that whatever is inside the dead garou is moving in such a way that it may start coming out of his dead mouth (remember large raven sitting on the things chest facing the dead garous face). The two GoF in Crinos (one with a spear , the other with an axe) state the following &quot; WERE GOING TO HACK THE SHIT OUT OF IT! (meaning the dead garou).<br /> <br /> ...Now , that being said, had the Get stated &quot; I knock the bird away, tell him to move, etc.. THEN I start hacking the body , OK no problem. Had they said &quot; I aim for the dead garous head or chest careful not to hit the corax , BOOM I aint got no problem.<br /> <br /> But they didn't do that. They said &quot; WE'RE GOING TO HACK THE SHIT OUT OF IT!&quot;.<br /> At that point I asked the Raven to dodge , I didn't even raise the difficulty for not facing the Get or anything.....mind you the players where at the same table , and start congratulating and high fiving...because theyre not paying attention what so fucking ever even after reminding them before the game and during the game TO PAY FUCKING ATTENTION.<br /> <br /> In retrospect to keep the game moving and save myself a headache I should have just said &quot; The bird moves out of the way&quot; or whatever. But I don't like playing WoD safe , and I really really don't like (no matter how much the players annoy me) taking over characters actions.<br /> <br /> I do have expectations , and its that the flavor and tone of the game is maintained and that people play maturely since its not some fantasy based D20 game. I even try to accommodate super silly ideas by helping the player come to a more reasonable conclusion by asking probing questions to the player. With these two problem players it was a waste of breathe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T11:43:34-08:00","id":1054391,"title":"","content":"One of the odd things to consider in WtA games is the idea of 'looting the bodies' takes on a completely different meaning when even the clothing of your enemy may be contaminated by the taint of the Wyrm. I generally rule that any object used by the servants of the Wyrm in the violation of another creature (or any object that housed an object used in the violation of another creature by a servant of the Wyrm) may be contaminated by the taint of the Wyrm. That means that the weapons of servants of the Wyrm should probably be destroyed to avoid allowing them to spread the taint of the Wyrm to innocent people and that the former apartment of a servant of the Wyrm may be so tainted by the violations performed by the previous tenant that anyone moving into the apartment will begin to suffer the taint of the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T12:09:16-08:00","id":1054404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054380#post1054380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If he had said that he just wanted teeth or a finger then I would have had no issue with it. And I do take some responsibility , its my game , but I have a certain expectation for players that have experience with storytelling games that you listen , think, and put yourself in the scene and your characters shoes so to speak. The problem is that this player just kept saying &amp;quot; I want the giants bones to make weapons!&amp;quot; I tried to probe further to help him come to the light and make a reasonable choice , but it never went that way with the player. Plus the bones were wyrm tainted , the pack was isolated in the wilderness with very very basic hiking gear and were on their way traveling twords the city. He didn't take talisman dedication , doesn't know rite of the fetish , doesn't know rite of cleansing etc......that being said....if it was a brand brand brand new player to the game I'd make allowances or introduce something to help the character out. This guy is not a new player to the game , he owns his own books....Im doubtful he reads anything except the &amp;quot; KEWL PW3RZ!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I dunno, just let him walk with the damn thing in his back on Crinos, give him a ton of penalties, make he delay the partie, until he realizes he's being stupid.<br /> <br /> The way I do: I tell the player the idea is stupid/absurd and give him the reasons, if he still insists, well, let him deal with the consequences. &quot;Yes, I wanna summon the Malfean! Are you sure? They are godlike creatures of death! Yes I'm sure! Gimme the dice! Ok...&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't like penalizing players, much less killing them, but utter stupidity must be rewarded.<br /> <br /> This looks a lot like the D&amp;D mindset... When I first started playing WoD, I would do it myself, I would think in terms of &quot;how much XP will I get if I kill the Prince?&quot;. But I was 12 (I'm 32 now), so eventually I learned that WoD wasn't about gaming powering to be able to desintegrate any weird stuff that the Game Master could concoct, but that it was about living in the shoes of your fictional character. And now, 20 years playing WoD, I know how to have have with this system, as well as I love playing D&amp;D too (and other too), in very different ways<br /> <br /> Maybe you could try having a serious talk with those guys before playing again to explain that, and also trying some different approach.<br /> <br /> And if it fails, don't play with them, it's a pity but it's better than being frustrated","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T12:30:07-08:00","id":1054410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054384#post1054384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to preface my explanation by saying that in my personal ST code , I don't like to babysit players and hand hold them , not when they have experience with the game. Furthermore it makes me uncomfortable as a ST to step in and tell a character &amp;quot; hey don't do that&amp;quot; or &amp;quot; hey do it like this&amp;quot; because I firmly believe in consequences , especially for not paying attention. Even more deeply , through personal experience( overseas and on the streets) I know that sometimes in the heat of battle , and as a response to fear and adrenaline , you will hit your own people , and sometimes it's lethal.<br /> <br /> I say that last thing to paint this picture: A dead garou was leaning against a large tree. Characters come upon it. Instead of healing him with mothers touch , they let him die. The massive Raven hops onto the dead garou's chest and starts pecking out an eye. While he is doing his Corax thing I state that something is rumbling inside the dead garou's chest and looks like its moving upinto the dead garou's throat. I as a ST left that open for a bit to see if the Corax says &amp;quot; Im going to fly away or hop off&amp;quot; , no such thing was stated. I then state that whatever is inside the dead garou is moving in such a way that it may start coming out of his dead mouth (remember large raven sitting on the things chest facing the dead garous face). The two GoF in Crinos (one with a spear , the other with an axe) state the following &amp;quot; WERE GOING TO HACK THE SHIT OUT OF IT! (meaning the dead garou).<br /> <br /> ...Now , that being said, had the Get stated &amp;quot; I knock the bird away, tell him to move, etc.. THEN I start hacking the body , OK no problem. Had they said &amp;quot; I aim for the dead garous head or chest careful not to hit the corax , BOOM I aint got no problem.<br /> <br /> But they didn't do that. They said &amp;quot; WE'RE GOING TO HACK THE SHIT OUT OF IT!&amp;quot;.<br /> At that point I asked the Raven to dodge , I didn't even raise the difficulty for not facing the Get or anything.....mind you the players where at the same table , and start congratulating and high fiving...because theyre not paying attention what so fucking ever even after reminding them before the game and during the game TO PAY FUCKING ATTENTION.<br /> <br /> In retrospect to keep the game moving and save myself a headache I should have just said &amp;quot; The bird moves out of the way&amp;quot; or whatever. But I don't like playing WoD safe , and I really really don't like (no matter how much the players annoy me) taking over characters actions.<br /> <br /> I do have expectations , and its that the flavor and tone of the game is maintained and that people play maturely since its not some fantasy based D20 game. I even try to accommodate super silly ideas by helping the player come to a more reasonable conclusion by asking probing questions to the player. With these two problem players it was a waste of breathe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand you. It is annoying indeed, when the players are not paying attention. And yes, I do agree that friendly fire happens on the heat of moment.<br /> <br /> However, the players can't see the scene, and sometimes, the scene that we, as ST, have in our head, is not the same as the player. I'm not saying you should babysitter your players. However, the players didn't said &quot;we hack the shit out of him toghether with the damn Raven!&quot;. It was clearly a mistake (by not paying attention, yes, but still, in their heads they weren't seeing the other player in the scene). <br /> <br /> First of all, I would've ask &quot;why didn't you HEAL the Metis&quot;? And secondly, I would've ask if they would hack the shit out of the dead body throw the corax player. Or, if you wanna reflect their poor choice in the heat of the moment, allow a roll of Wits+Alertness to <i>remember</i> them of the situation before they made their retard move.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying those players are not bad, I'm just saying you don't need to be so harsh. And, why were the Corax just standing there with a bovine calm while there were an Alien bursting from the corpse? It seems he weren't so great either in that one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T12:42:55-08:00","id":1054419,"title":"","content":"I appreciate your responses Karlsgust they've given me a lot to ponder. All your suggestions would have been viable. I should intervene in small ways with the interest of the overall game. I coulda handled it a couple different ways. I let my temper get the better of me by getting too attached to my vision. Fuck my friends though in the long run, no more WtA for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T12:49:59-08:00","id":1054425,"title":"","content":"Hindsight is always 20-20. As an ST you have to make an instant decision. It's easy for us to nitpick your ST choices from a distance and with more than a few seconds to make a decision. <br /> <br /> I'd let the player have the bones, give them disturbing dreams, and have the elders go &quot;WTF are you doing bring those tainted things into the Caern, cliath?&quot; Maybe even make it into plot. &quot;Thanks to you dumb asses, we got a bunch of banes heading our way.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T13:17:36-08:00","id":1054441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054391#post1054391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I generally rule that any object used by the servants of the Wyrm in the violation of another creature (or any object that housed an object used in the violation of another creature by a servant of the Wyrm) may be contaminated by the taint of the Wyrm. That means that the weapons of servants of the Wyrm should probably be destroyed to avoid allowing them to spread the taint of the Wyrm to innocent people and that the former apartment of a servant of the Wyrm may be so tainted by the violations performed by the previous tenant that anyone moving into the apartment will begin to suffer the taint of the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div> Rite of Cleansing works to fix both of those examples. And it's an incredibly common, low level Rite.<br /> <br /> Edit: adding to that thought: because it's low level, it shouldn't work to cleanse Bane Fetishes by any means, since they are effectively powered by an internal Wyrm taint battery (the spirit) so that could still be a factor in the idea of &quot;looting the bodies&quot;.<br /> <br /> But yea...general body parts or locations should be fair game. And if the dead creature were really heavily tainted, the body parts might just dissolve in the Rite leaving nothing to work with.<br /> <br /> I have yet to be in a Werewolf game where the Rite of Cleansing wasn't used at least somewhat liberally after encounters with Wyrm creatures.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 02-24-2017, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T13:23:11-08:00","id":1054443,"title":"","content":"Another thing to consider would be to have the contaminated bones create Mental Taints in the people who are carrying them because their greed gives Vorus, the Urge of Greed, a channel to corrupt them. Every day, secretly roll the Willpower of the Garou who is carrying them, at a difficulty 6, with them suffering Mental Taint associated with Greed if they fail their Willpower roll. <br /> <br /> After they suffer the Mental Taint of Greed, you require them to make a Wits plus Primal Urge roll, difficulty 6, to avoid giving into their greed for a scene. If they spend a point of Willpower, they can control themselves for a turn. In addition, Vorus would whisper into the ear of the character, trying to corrupt them, and the character would have to succeed on a Wits plus Enigmas roll (difficulty 8 [difficulty 6 if he is aware of the nature of the Urge Wyrms]) to realize that the thoughts are not his own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T13:56:06-08:00","id":1054455,"title":"","content":"As a former problem player, I'd like to offer some things that caused me to be one;<br /> <br /> -The ever lovely difference between books and the group's playstyle. As well as edition confusion.<br /> <br /> -Being the newbie, therefore not understanding everything fully.<br /> <br /> - No previous ties to the group and coming in late in the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T17:58:10-08:00","id":1054540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054443#post1054443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing to consider would be to have the contaminated bones create Mental Taints in the people who are carrying them because their greed gives Vorus, the Urge of Greed, a channel to corrupt them. Every day, secretly roll the Willpower of the Garou who is carrying them, at a difficulty 6, with them suffering Mental Taint associated with Greed if they fail their Willpower roll. <br /> <br /> After they suffer the Mental Taint of Greed, you require them to make a Wits plus Primal Urge roll, difficulty 6, to avoid giving into their greed for a scene. If they spend a point of Willpower, they can control themselves for a turn. In addition, Vorus would whisper into the ear of the character, trying to corrupt them, and the character would have to succeed on a Wits plus Enigmas roll (difficulty 8 [difficulty 6 if he is aware of the nature of the Urge Wyrms]) to realize that the thoughts are not his own.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty cool I'm going to keep this in my back pocket if I ever forgive my shitty buddy (still my boy but damnit if he doesn't aggravate me when we game)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T17:59:03-08:00","id":1054542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054455#post1054455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a former problem player, I'd like to offer some things that caused me to be one;<br /> <br /> -The ever lovely difference between books and the group's playstyle. As well as edition confusion.<br /> <br /> -Being the newbie, therefore not understanding everything fully.<br /> <br /> - No previous ties to the group and coming in late in the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>How did your problem player issues manifest? Just curious...I'm now trying to think if I was one or not<br /> <br /> I know I can become a shitty ST when I get loaded during games but that's the parties fault for filling me with goodies when we get together. It's probably because I start throwing XP around like crazy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12902,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","user":"WISDOMINCHAINS","date":". 02-24-2017, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T18:05:40-08:00","id":1054545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054425#post1054425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd let the player have the bones, give them disturbing dreams, and have the elders go &quot;WTF are you doing bring those tainted things into the Caern, cliath?&quot; Maybe even make it into plot. &quot;Thanks to you dumb asses, we got a bunch of banes heading our way.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI love this kind of stuff. I was going to write more than what I'm going to write now, because <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12880\" data-vbnamecard=\"12880\">Karlgust</a> made some similar points to what I was thinking, but I'll still add in a bit.<br /> <br /> First, one of the best pieces of advice I've ever received as a gamer AND a ST/GM is: &quot;Don't say no to another player.&quot; Note, that's not the same as, &quot;Don't say no to another character.&quot; And, also keep in mind that this is coming from a place of, &quot;What can we do to make this player have fun?&quot; That doesn't mean the player/character gets away with everything willy-nilly. In the scenario <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3950_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3950\" data-vbnamecard=\"3950\">wonderandawe</a> gave, not saying no causes some cool story shit to happen. Similarly, it's also not the same as, &quot;Give them their way.&quot; In this particular case, the &quot;Don't say no&quot; concept could simply be turned into, &quot;Okay. What part of what bone are you trying to take?&quot; Limit him without outright denying him. If he has a laundry list of bone pieces, as soon as he gets one or two, say that the rest of the skeleton starts turning into dust and soil. Manifestation of an earth elemental, after all! If the bone pieces he now has ever touches earth again, have them do the same (just to carry through with the story). If he starts asking a bunch of ridiculous questions to challenge why you did that, shrug and smile and say, &quot;Good question. Perhaps ask your Theurge.&quot; Or whatever. Push the scene back into RP.<br /> <br /> Second, my last long-running group had a problem player who sounds a lot like this guy. We ultimately had to part ways with him, but that was because he was only showing up to half the games. What helped curb his dumbassery was advice brilliantly put by our ST: &quot;Okay, interesting idea. But first, I want you to think: what is likely to happen if you SUCCEED?&quot; Often, players like this just get caught up in Moon Moon's &quot;GONDA DO THING, GONDA GET THING!&quot; style of excitement. Reign them in by making them think about the consequences of their actions. In attacking the body, it's that nudge of, &quot;What will happen if you succeed?&quot; // &quot;We'll kill whatever THAT is!&quot; // &quot;You might hit your friend. You might miss whatever it is that's about to happen, because you don't know what's happening.&quot; If they really are that trigger happy, then give them another situation when they act first and think later, only this time, they've lost a critical key to their goal in the process. Whoops. Shit's about to get a lot harder, and now you've pissed off your pack. Then let the pack handle it! With said problem player in our group? I whacked him with a Falling Touch one time when he was about to do something that would get us unnecessarily hurt (... I was playing a Ragabash, so it was also rather amusing to him as a character). The character (and probably the player) was pissy about it, but guess what? It stopped him enough to think about his actions.<br /> <br /> If two players are being peas in a pod, don't let them sit next to each other, for one (and be honest and tell them it's 'cause they get disruptive together). And, second, maybe encourage one of them to make a new character who is considerably different than the other's (and different than their current attitudes). They're both Get? Sounds like they're both just wanting to run around smashing the thing. If they encourage their Moon Moon behavior, alter their presence at the table.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, though, they may just not be a good fit for the game.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://68.media.tumblr.com/8df352586976d8a85cef69d67a303cba/tumblr_inline_n0sppbvcfG1rkuwow.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://68.media.tumblr.com/8df352586976d8a85cef69d67a303cba/tumblr_inline_n0sppbvcfG1rkuwow.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://68.media.tumblr.com/8df352586976d8a85cef69d67a303cba/tumblr_inline_n0sppbvcfG1rkuwow.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://68.media.tumblr.com/8df352586976d8a85cef69d67a303cba/tumblr_inline_n0sppbvcfG1rkuwow.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user