ing to him as a character). The character (and probably the player) was pissy about it, but guess what? It stopped him enough to think about his actions.<br /> <br /> If two players are being peas in a pod, don't let them sit next to each other, for one (and be honest and tell them it's 'cause they get disruptive together). And, second, maybe encourage one of them to make a new character who is considerably different than the other's (and different than their current attitudes). They're both Get? Sounds like they're both just wanting to run around smashing the thing. If they encourage their Moon Moon behavior, alter their presence at the table.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, though, they may just not be a good fit for the game.<br /> <a href=\"http://68.media.tumblr.com/8df352586976d8a85cef69d67a303cba/tumblr_inline_n0sppbvcfG1rkuwow.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://68.media.tumblr.com/8df352586...cfG1rkuwow.jpg</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Man thank you so much for this, this is giving me even more to think about , spot on. <br /> <br /> Funny thing is this buddy of mine, the rest of the players started calling him moon moon...I had no idea what they were referring too at the time but went with it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T18:38:34-08:00","id":1054567,"title":"","content":"Though as a warning, you'll have to watch out for those players who realize the ST is annoyed and may come up with plot later for thier new toy. These players then proceed to spend the next hour of game coming up with paranoid schemes to secure thier prize so the ST doesn't &quot;fuck them over&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T18:43:03-08:00","id":1054570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054567#post1054567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though as a warning, you'll have to watch out for those players who realize the ST is annoyed and may come up with plot later for thier new toy. These players then proceed to spend the next hour of game coming up with paranoid schemes to secure thier prize so the ST doesn't &amp;quot;fuck them over&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm intrigued but don't really get it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T18:52:51-08:00","id":1054576,"title":"","content":"Basically, these players want thier Ill gotten loot without any consequences. So they derail game so they can counter any plans the ST can come up with. <br /> <br /> I see it alot with D&amp;D players. Player/dungeon master relationship in Pathfinder and D&amp;D is different than in white wolf games. In white wolf, you are creating a story together. Stories have conflict and problems for the players to solve. In D&amp;D, the DM is trying to kill you. <br /> <br /> After years of running White Wolf games, I ran a pathfinder game. My players would complain I was too soft. They wanted me to try and do my best to kill the whole party. It was completely different from the way I ran all my previous games. It took a bit to get used to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T19:06:21-08:00","id":1054582,"title":"","content":"How does that not become extremely boring","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T19:10:58-08:00","id":1054585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054582#post1054582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does that not become extremely boring</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the same question, to be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T19:15:24-08:00","id":1054588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054576#post1054576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I see it alot with D&amp;D players. Player/dungeon master relationship in Pathfinder and D&amp;D is different than in white wolf games. In white wolf, you are creating a story together. Stories have conflict and problems for the players to solve. In D&amp;D, the DM is trying to kill you.<br /> <br /> After years of running White Wolf games, I ran a pathfinder game. My players would complain I was too soft. They wanted me to try and do my best to kill the whole party. It was completely different from the way I ran all my previous games. It took a bit to get used to.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has never been my experience with D&amp;D, though I've heard of this outlook before and I always found that portrayal odd.<br /> <br /> I guess maybe it's because the core of my gaming group for both systems tended to be the same and so we played both games similarly. Creating an interesting and memorable story has always been more important than what monsters you can kill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054582#post1054582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does that not become extremely boring</div> </div> </div> </div>It really does seem boring. Constant combat always is.<br /> And there is no reason the person running the game can't just kill the players if they feel like it (in any system really), so it's just kind of an odd concept, having the ST/DM &quot;try and kill the PCs&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 02-24-2017, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T19:24:52-08:00","id":1054590,"title":"","content":"We came to a compromise. I ran the plot how I wanted and did my best to kill the party. My players had a great time with the rp, though I think my power gamer got bored and only can to game because his girlfriend enjoyed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T20:46:25-08:00","id":1054619,"title":"","content":"Combat in D&amp;D is more of a way of life than it is in WoD, even compared to WtA. Because the players outnumber you, it's important that you try to kill them in order to make the puzzle of surviving hard enough for the players to find it interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T20:53:21-08:00","id":1054623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054619#post1054619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combat in D&amp;D is more of a way of life than it is in WoD, even compared to WtA. Because the players outnumber you, it's important that you try to kill them in order to make the puzzle of surviving hard enough for the players to find it interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how it was explained to me. <br /> <br /> However this mindset creates a boring WoD game. I'm used to players embracing thier characters' flaws and making non optimal choices because it is in character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T21:25:11-08:00","id":1054634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054542#post1054542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How did your problem player issues manifest? Just curious...I'm now trying to think if I was one or not<br /> <br /> I know I can become a shitty ST when I get loaded during games but that's the parties fault for filling me with goodies when we get together. It's probably because I start throwing XP around like crazy</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguing with the ST a lot, mostly because they saw my previous roleplaying experience (non-dice forum and chat roleplay) as not 'true' roleplay. And by not getting everything right away (I read the books, didn't know the system well). With hindsight, I should have left before the ST enforced a strict non-artwork character picture policy (it was played on a forum, note).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T22:19:53-08:00","id":1054649,"title":"","content":"WtA is probably the most combat heavy cWoD game, and I have run sessions where the body count among the enemy was much higher than anything you would find in a Pathfinder game. With their high soaks and their regeneration, Garou tend to be capable of taking on infantry platoons without difficulty if they are smart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-25-2017, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T16:12:04-08:00","id":1059261,"title":"","content":"another bullshit thing I heard from the same problem playyer, was calling Erebus &quot;torture &amp; brainwashing&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T16:39:50-08:00","id":1059270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059261#post1059261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">another bullshit thing I heard from the same problem playyer, was calling Erebus &amp;quot;torture &amp; brainwashing&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... Its not so much bullshit...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T17:46:01-08:00","id":1059287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1054588#post1054588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has never been my experience with D&amp;D, though I've heard of this outlook before and I always found that portrayal odd.<br /> <br /> I guess maybe it's because the core of my gaming group for both systems tended to be the same and so we played both games similarly. Creating an interesting and memorable story has always been more important than what monsters you can kill.<br /> <br /> <br /> It really does seem boring. Constant combat always is.<br /> And there is no reason the person running the game can't just kill the players if they feel like it (in any system really), so it's just kind of an odd concept, having the ST/DM &quot;try and kill the PCs&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> in a white howler game at the Grand Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <br /> I asked the ST &quot;wait, a group of rank 4 garou are the youngest pack at the sept?&quot; <br /> <br /> and he replied with a irritated &quot;whos running the game?&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> it can be hard to tell when a point is legitimate <br /> <br /> oh anyone run a first team that are graduates of <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ImperialStormtrooperMarksmanshipAcademy\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...manshipAcademy</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T06:02:52-08:00","id":1059459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059261#post1059261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">another bullshit thing I heard from the same problem playyer, was calling Erebus &quot;torture &amp; brainwashing&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a totally fair opinion. WTA is the story of a group of cultists from a family of trigger-happy shapeshifters, who obey the commands of powerful spirits almost unquestioningly and can only LEVEL UP if they say &quot;how high&quot; when they are told to jump. There's no escaping that. Embrace it. It's really fucked up, even if it's True. WTA is the story of a person turning into a wolf/human for the first time and suddenly being Drafted into an army to Destroy (laughs into the void since that's both paradoxical and impossible) the corrupted force of Destruction which is consuming the Earth. If you refuse the call you're a coward, you're worse than a traitor, you're nothing.<br /> <br /> I'm perfectly okay with all of that, I fully accept that WTA is at least a tad authoritarian and creepy and cultish. The issue seems to be that many WTA players and STs missed the memo. &quot;Oh, it's okay because the lore says it's okay. They're right so it's alright.&quot; Firstly, that sounds like propaganda. Secondly &quot;don't worry young one, us Elders/Ancestors/Spirits did the thinking for you&quot; is pretty much textbook indoctrination. WTA, RAW, is incredibly nuanced and interesting. The common interpretation seems to be somewhat lacking from what I have read, as it skims over uncomfortable aspects for the purposes of escapism and empowerment. And that's okay! Your game doesn't have to have internal conflict or internalized nuance, the conflict and nuance can be totally external... but you'd be disingenuous if you said that &quot;oh, you've become too focused on Order and Logic, into the river of burning silver you go&quot; and &quot;well done for blowing up that factory which employs 100s of innocents on the edge of poverty and brings capitol to an entire community, have some Renown&quot; are entirely natural and not-fucked-up things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-07-2017, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T06:44:43-08:00","id":1059474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059261#post1059261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">another bullshit thing I heard from the same problem playyer, was calling Erebus &quot;torture &amp; brainwashing&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree. It would be like saying that surgery to remove a terminal cancer was 'an unnecessary violation of the holistic integrity of the body'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T06:48:16-08:00","id":1059475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059474#post1059474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to agree. It would be like saying that surgery to remove a terminal cancer was 'an unnecessary violation of the holistic integrity of the body'.</div> </div> </div> </div>A cancerous lump isn't a set of legitimate opinions and beliefs. A Werewolf who gets overly attached to the Wyld doesn't need &quot;correcting&quot;, they simply have different beliefs to those around them. If that cannot be tolerated and they are forced into Erebus, that is a totalitarian theocracy with torture and brainwashing, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:11:00-08:00","id":1059484,"title":"","content":"I doubt that Erebus could burn off excess Weaver energies or Wyld energies, so any Garou that tried to toss other Garou into the silver lake for excess Weaver energies or Wyld energies would likely find themselves tossed in the lake instead by the guardians of Erebus because of their Wyrm Taint. The problem that Erebus is designed to solve is Wyrm Taint because there is no logical or rational argument for the Wyrm. The Wyrm is the corruption of the natural order and, like an aggressive cancer, its tumors must be surgically removed if the patient is to have any chance at survival.<br /> <br /> I really do not understand the objection to Erebus because Erebus is a wonderful place that purifies Garou of their corruption while they are alive (the only other alternative is an honorable death in battle or a dishonorable descent into madness and perversion). I have had entire groups travel to Erebus to willingly subject themselves to Erebus after they were contaminated by Wyrm Taint. It is a place of purification through suffering, and the Garou are always willing to suffer for the greater good (and those that are not willing to suffer will probably see things differently after Erebus purifies them of their Wyrm Taint).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:27:24-08:00","id":1059491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059484#post1059484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt that Erebus could burn off excess Weaver energies or Wyld energies, so any Garou that tried to toss other Garou into the silver lake for excess Weaver energies or Wyld energies would likely find themselves tossed in the lake instead by the guardians of Erebus because of their Wyrm Taint. The problem that Erebus is designed to solve is Wyrm Taint because there is no logical or rational argument for the Wyrm. The Wyrm is the corruption of the natural order and, like an aggressive cancer, its tumors must be surgically removed if the patient is to have any chance at survival.<br /> <br /> I really do not understand the objection to Erebus because Erebus is a wonderful place that purifies Garou of their corruption while they are alive (the only other alternative is an honorable death in battle or a dishonorable descent into madness and perversion). I have had entire groups travel to Erebus to willingly subject themselves to Erebus after they were contaminated by Wyrm Taint. It is a place of purification through suffering, and the Garou are always willing to suffer for the greater good (and those that are not willing to suffer will probably see things differently after Erebus purifies them of their Wyrm Taint).</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Often compared to <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Garou\" target=\"_blank\">Garou</a> &quot;hell&quot;, <b>Erebus</b> is actually a place of spiritual cleansing. Erebus is filled with rivers of molten silver which both burn and heal at the same time, extending the torment of the inmates for months, years, possibly even centuries.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Werewolves end up in Erebus when they have become too <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Taint_(cWOD)\" target=\"_blank\">tainted</a> by one of the members of the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Triat\" target=\"_blank\">Triat</a>, most often the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Wyrm\" target=\"_blank\">Wyrm</a>. Either the werewolf will journey to Erebus to be cleansed, or will be dragged there by other werewolves.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:29:04-08:00","id":1059493,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> So yes, &quot;Dave is too Wyld-obsessed&quot; is a totally fair reason (RAW) for his pack to drag him to Erebus and throw him in. And that could lead to decades of psychological torture as his beliefs which emphasize the Wyld over the rest of the Triat and Gaia (his deep-held religious beliefs) are presumably washed away. If only we had a word for washing away someone's psychological convictions using artificial methods...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:39:54-08:00","id":1059498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mKrknumPym8\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mKrknumPym8\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mKrknumPym8\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mKrknumPym8 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:40:53-08:00","id":1059499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059484#post1059484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really do not understand the objection to Erebus because Erebus is a wonderful place that purifies Garou of their corruption while they are alive (the only other alternative is an honorable death in battle or a dishonorable descent into madness and perversion). I have had entire groups travel to Erebus to willingly subject themselves to Erebus after they were contaminated by Wyrm Taint. It is a place of purification through suffering, and the Garou are always willing to suffer for the greater good (and those that are not willing to suffer will probably see things differently after Erebus purifies them of their Wyrm Taint).</div> </div> </div> </div>Boiling in a lake of liquid silver that also magically boosts your regeneration so that you can neither die nor escape is not &quot;wonderful&quot;. I am utterly baffled that <i><i>anyone</i></i> believes Garou can come out of Erebus sane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:43:58-08:00","id":1059500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059498#post1059498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mKrknumPym8\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mKrknumPym8</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Crying. Seriously, don't know what I was expecting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:48:32-08:00","id":1059505,"title":"","content":"I imagine Garou are sent to Erebus only in situations where the Garou Nation would otherwise kill the Garou for their actions. Yet for some reason the Philodox believe the Garou is worth saving. Either because they have knowledge/skills/renown or perhaps the Garou was a packmate who was forced to dance the Spiral and now wishes to repent. <br /> <br /> A Garou will come back from Erebus changed beyond just removing the Taint. Surviving Erebus is a harrowing experience. The effects on the character should be more than erasing Wyrm taint from the character sheet.<br /> <br /> Of course, now I have an Elder NPC idea brewing in my head. He went to Erebus and came back changed. Not sure why he went there or how he changed. The idea is still baking in my brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:48:40-08:00","id":1059506,"title":"","content":"I would argue that, if my memory doesn't fail me, Taint in a level that warrant's a horrifying travel to Erebus it's not ever caused by &quot;an opinion&quot;, (much less a valid one) but a spiritual alteration akin to having lepra in your soul. Erebus it's not a place where you get sended just because you &quot;smell of the wyrm/weaver/wyld&quot; or have a convoluted oppinion. There are much less extreme or dangerous ways to eradicate low level taint that don't alter the way you think in any way. Thus &quot;brainwashing by torture&quot; doesn't seem to be a correct decription of the place, it's more a &quot;ordeal to heal your soul&quot; kind of thing.<br /> <br /> But I disgress, thinking that &quot;Werewolf it's dumb/bad&quot; doesn't make one a &quot;problem player&quot;, it merely makes one to be a &quot;player that doesn't like werewolf&quot; (which it's problematic if you want to play that particular game, but nothing more)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:53:20-08:00","id":1059508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059506#post1059506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I disgress, thinking that &quot;Werewolf it's dumb/bad&quot; doesn't make one a &quot;problem player&quot;, it merely makes one to be a &quot;player that doesn't like werewolf&quot; (which it's problematic if you want to play that particular game, but nothing more)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree. If you dislike Spirits and the Umbra, and hate Werewolves, maybe WTA isn't the game for you. I actually love WTA as it is presented, simply because of how horrifically fucked up it is if you think about things for more than a minute. There's something entertaining about the feeling of Heroism you get from it, even if you know that the perspective of your character is incredibly screwed up and weird. I enjoy blowing up a factory as a Glass Walker for the same reason that I love turning a rival Vampire into a tapestry in VTM, they're both &quot;I did it!&quot; moments which are utterly monstrous. WTA is just extra delicious since you're surrounded by NPCs and PCs who don't think they're monsters, which makes it more enjoyable IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:05:28-08:00","id":1059521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059508#post1059508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd agree. If you dislike Spirits and the Umbra, and hate Werewolves, maybe WTA isn't the game for you. I actually love WTA as it is presented, simply because of how horrifically fucked up it is if you think about things for more than a minute. There's something entertaining about the feeling of Heroism you get from it, even if you know that the perspective of your character is incredibly screwed up and weird. I enjoy blowing up a factory as a Glass Walker for the same reason that I love turning a rival Vampire into a tapestry in VTM, they're both &quot;I did it!&quot; moments which are utterly monstrous. WTA is just extra delicious since you're surrounded by NPCs and PCs who don't think they're monsters, which makes it more enjoyable IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Man, I love playing characters with a different moral code. A Garou does have a moral compass, it just doesn't point true north. Or maybe it does point true north and all us normal people are selfish bastards for wanting to work for a living, raise our children, and maybe not getting ripped to shreds for eating fast food.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:18:00-08:00","id":1059527,"title":"","content":"W20 Changed Erebus byaxing the other changing breeds equilvents, now its built out of the collective karmic debt of the garou. for the war of rage and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T08:22:36-08:00","id":1059530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059521#post1059521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Man, I love playing characters with a different moral code. A Garou does have a moral compass, it just doesn't point true north. Or maybe it does point true north and all us normal people are selfish bastards for wanting to work for a living, raise our children, and maybe not getting ripped to shreds for eating fast food.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take? The very state of being which is Garou is a Path of Enlightenment wrapped in the Appeal to Nature and Appeal to Tradition fallacies. It's utterly inhumane, monstrous and not something humans should aspire to (hence Hunters being a thing), and Garou thinking they're more moral than Kindred (and those filthy Quintessence-hunting Mages, and those freaky Fae, and those Demons and Ghosts) is simply a matter of perspective. Is it worse to turn one other monster into a quilt, or is it worse to blow up a factory and kill 10 random security guards? Is it worse to mind-control a human until they kill their family, or kill a whole community by wiping out the oil refinery they rely upon? There are no concrete answers to these questions, which is why I like playing ANY role which puts me in an inhuman and monstrous perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-07-2017, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T09:31:30-08:00","id":1059571,"title":"","content":"But here is the thing, is it immoral to destroy the oil refinery if it is creating poisons that turn innocent workers and innocent customers into Fomori? I mean, I feel for the 10,000 people whose community is ruined by the closing of the refinery, but their suffering pales in comparison to the 10,000 people per year that the products of the refinery will turn into Fomori, some of whom will be members of that community. The Garou do not fight against humanity, they fight against the Wyrm for all life (including humanity), it is just that humans are willing to accept a world that promotes the Wyrm without many questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T09:57:48-08:00","id":1059583,"title":"","content":"As someone who plays a character who went for an Erebus dip, you cannot redeem until you forgive yourself. Aka, it is more akin to the purgatory than hell.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> - I agree that garou are effed up, but I think at times in a solely WtA game bringing it up does not really do any good. The best example of garou arrogance and pride I actually got from playing in a low-level crossover game. There, when surrounded by unseelie fae, former Faith 5 hunter and a sorceress, the two garou and how they acted contrasted heavily with their non-ragey teammates. Impulsive, biased, inhuman and jaded by their core nature, they creeped out their teammates up at times. And cameoing my other garou characters at times there made me rethink these characters. How easily my Silver Fang galliard, who typically was very polite and nice, was insulting and petty towards the two ronin in the team.<br /> <br /> Aka, you need to have an outsider perspective at least at part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T10:26:08-08:00","id":1059597,"title":"","content":"And you can never seek redemption, or forgive yourself, after you Walk the Spiral. There are three BSD beneath the silver lake, and they have been there for centuries because they seek neither redemption or forgiveness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T10:33:36-08:00","id":1059602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059571#post1059571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But here is the thing, is it immoral to destroy the oil refinery if it is creating poisons that turn innocent workers and innocent customers into Fomori? I mean, I feel for the 10,000 people whose community is ruined by the closing of the refinery, but their suffering pales in comparison to the 10,000 people per year that the products of the refinery will turn into Fomori, some of whom will be members of that community. The Garou do not fight against humanity, they fight against the Wyrm for all life (including humanity), it is just that humans are willing to accept a world that promotes the Wyrm without many questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that comes in with some assumptions. One assumption is that animals matter. The environment definitely matters, but Garou seem to think that the Biosphere MUST be a certain way, that there's a correct degree of human population around the world, and that every community of animals matters, even if killing them greatly improves human quality of life. Even taking spirits into account I think the Garou's view of the world is horrific; look at extremist animal right's activists, the kind who argue that if humans and animals are equal, killing one human to save hundreds of animals is perfectly okay. Those are common right? No, they aren't common, because very few people are that twisted or inhumane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T10:51:35-08:00","id":1059608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059583#post1059583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who plays a character who went for an Erebus dip, you cannot redeem until you forgive yourself. Aka, it is more akin to the purgatory than hell.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> - I agree that garou are effed up, but I think at times in a solely WtA game bringing it up does not really do any good. The best example of garou arrogance and pride I actually got from playing in a low-level crossover game. There, when surrounded by unseelie fae, former Faith 5 hunter and a sorceress, the two garou and how they acted contrasted heavily with their non-ragey teammates. Impulsive, biased, inhuman and jaded by their core nature, they creeped out their teammates up at times. And cameoing my other garou characters at times there made me rethink these characters. How easily my Silver Fang galliard, who typically was very polite and nice, was insulting and petty towards the two ronin in the team.<br /> <br /> Aka, you need to have an outsider perspective at least at part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Antagonists and allies give outsider perspectives, at least that's how I do things. Vampires have to listen to people like Sullivan &quot;why haven't you met the sun?&quot; Dane. He's genuinely curious, not hateful, he just can't understand why Vampires don't just walk into the sun and end it. You can work opposition to the Gaian Theocracy into a purely Werewolf game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T11:19:49-08:00","id":1059620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059484#post1059484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt that Erebus could burn off excess Weaver energies or Wyld energies, so any Garou that tried to toss other Garou into the silver lake for excess Weaver energies or Wyld energies would likely find themselves tossed in the lake instead by the guardians of Erebus because of their Wyrm Taint. The problem that Erebus is designed to solve is Wyrm Taint because there is no logical or rational argument for the Wyrm. The Wyrm is the corruption of the natural order and, like an aggressive cancer, its tumors must be surgically removed if the patient is to have any chance at survival.<br /> <br /> I really do not understand the objection to Erebus because Erebus is a wonderful place that purifies Garou of their corruption while they are alive (the only other alternative is an honorable death in battle or a dishonorable descent into madness and perversion). I have had entire groups travel to Erebus to willingly subject themselves to Erebus after they were contaminated by Wyrm Taint. It is a place of purification through suffering, and the Garou are always willing to suffer for the greater good (and those that are not willing to suffer will probably see things differently after Erebus purifies them of their Wyrm Taint).</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I also heard that fire is an excelent purifocation for the soul; the Inquisition proved that when it purified all those wiches souls... Thank God for that, otherwise their souls would be with Satan now.<br /> <br /> Right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T11:22:04-08:00","id":1059623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059493#post1059493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> So yes, &amp;quot;Dave is too Wyld-obsessed&amp;quot; is a totally fair reason (RAW) for his pack to drag him to Erebus and throw him in. And that could lead to decades of psychological torture as his beliefs which emphasize the Wyld over the rest of the Triat and Gaia (his deep-held religious beliefs) are presumably washed away. If only we had a word for washing away someone's psychological convictions using artificial methods...</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, isn't agonizing torture a very valid way of convincing people to change their minds about something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T11:24:27-08:00","id":1059625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059499#post1059499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boiling in a lake of liquid silver that also magically boosts your regeneration so that you can neither die nor escape is not &amp;quot;wonderful&amp;quot;. I am utterly baffled that <i><i>anyone</i></i> believes Garou can come out of Erebus sane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its called &quot;Lobotomagic&quot;.<br /> <br /> No Brain, No Pain","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T11:26:40-08:00","id":1059628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059623#post1059623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, isn't agonizing torture a very valid way of convincing people to change their minds about something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, my Bahari NPCs certainly feel that way, but I don't think that's a mainstream opinion ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T11:29:07-08:00","id":1059629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059620#post1059620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, I also heard that fire is an excelent purifocation for the soul; the Inquisition proved that when it purified all those wiches souls... Thank God for that, otherwise their souls would be with Satan now.<br /> <br /> Right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Difference being the witches got ashed and the Garou literally cannot die in Erebus.<br /> <br /> Pain is not evil. Pain is a tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T11:30:12-08:00","id":1059630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059506#post1059506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that, if my memory doesn't fail me, Taint in a level that warrant's a horrifying travel to Erebus it's not ever caused by &amp;quot;an opinion&amp;quot;, (much less a valid one) but a spiritual alteration akin to having lepra in your soul. Erebus it's not a place where you get sended just because you &amp;quot;smell of the wyrm/weaver/wyld&amp;quot; or have a convoluted oppinion. There are much less extreme or dangerous ways to eradicate low level taint that don't alter the way you think in any way. Thus &amp;quot;brainwashing by torture&amp;quot; doesn't seem to be a correct decription of the place, it's more a &amp;quot;ordeal to heal your soul&amp;quot; kind of thing.<br /> <br /> But I disgress, thinking that &amp;quot;Werewolf it's dumb/bad&amp;quot; doesn't make one a &amp;quot;problem player&amp;quot;, it merely makes one to be a &amp;quot;player that doesn't like werewolf&amp;quot; (which it's problematic if you want to play that particular game, but nothing more)</div> </div> </div> </div>By that description, you just said that a place like the Christian hell is a good thing.<br /> <br /> Oh, all those sinners back there, they are wicked and evil, Satan worshippers, so its obviously a good thing that they burn and suffer and beg and cry, because their souls are tainted, they didnt followed the laws of the Lord, so to burn in hell is a perfect expression of our God perfect goodness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T11:36:14-08:00","id":1059634,"title":"","content":"to sum it up, my experience with the girl in question aol, back when their were a fair share of White wolf RPs there (Many very bad) is an example of why &quot;Learning the setting with your charachter&quot; while it can be exciating and fun, is a very dicey proposition, if they find out its something they done care for,, and she BOMBARDED me with bullshit ideas for changes, make the Umbra a &quot;Alternate dimension the governments using for nuclear weapons tests, King albrecht a pawn of the CIA, and other assorted bullshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T11:44:27-08:00","id":1059640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059629#post1059629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Difference being the witches got ashed and the Garou literally cannot die in Erebus.<br /> <br /> Pain is not evil. Pain is a tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pain is a tool?<br /> <br /> Oh my god, Im finding all the modern days inquisitors<br /> <br /> Look, I share the opinions of 11twiggins. I think its ok for the <i>fictional</i> Garou to have those... Disturbing ideas.<br /> <br /> They are monsters after all! Its part of the fun play with those inhuman beasts who share monstruous believes.<br /> <br /> But, what really disturbes me is how the players take those ideas of the game as their own. How can you ADVOCATE PAIN?<br /> <br /> Hey, why dont we torture all those lost souls inside our prisons? Right? We should torture them all, until we can &quot;CURE&quot; them!!! Wouldn't that be awesome? They are all &quot;tainted&quot; after all right?<br /> <br /> Right?<br /> <br /> Well, pain is a tool, I dont see why can't we use it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T11:49:20-08:00","id":1059642,"title":"","content":"Originally, there is no such thing as the Christian Hell (at least not beyond the idea of Tartarus for the fallen angels). If you look at the original texts of the Old Testament and the New Testament in the Ancient Greek, you will see that the first Christians did not worry about Hell because Hell did not exist for mortals. The idea of Hell for mortals came as pagan beliefs were incorporated into Christian doctrines and as late Roman Church leaders, who restricted access to the Bible to the elites and the priesthood, decided to use the threat of Hell and Damnation as a motivation to increase conversion to Christianity (and to gain wealth and political power). The Medieval and Modern Church simply followed the lead of the late Roman Church because they found it was easier to promote conversion (and to gain wealth and political power) as long as they threatened people with Hell and Damnation.<br /> <br /> Erebus is a wonderful resource for the Garou. If they feel that they have committed a sin, they can subject themselves to the silver of Erebus in order to cleanse the taint from their souls and to gain forgiveness. On a more personal level, what mortal would not desire a place like Erebus, where they could find true cleansing and true forgiveness through their suffering while they are alive and could return to the world of living? I would not hesitate for a second to enter Erebus if I was guaranteed the cleansing and the forgiveness that the Garou receive from their suffering (and the guarantee that I would return to the world of the living).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T11:50:45-08:00","id":1059644,"title":"","content":"Hey, I even find a hell of a fun to play with Red Talons (my favorite tribe), they just wanna rip humans off, and thats it.<br /> <br /> And... They ALSO dont think they are villains or monsters.<br /> <br /> And thats how ALL the Gaian theocracy should be seem BY THE PLAYERS.<br /> <br /> As an evil death cult.<br /> <br /> You know, real life terrorists also think they are blessed heroes doing the will of god or fighting for a better world.<br /> <br /> Thats how I see werewolves, as fanatics on a evil death cult, and that to me is OK.<br /> <br /> I dont see why thats a problemas, but I think its disturbing to see people that admire this kind of insanity (no, killing people is NEVER a good thing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:00:02-08:00","id":1059649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059642#post1059642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Originally, there is no such thing as the Christian Hell (at least not beyond the idea of Tartarus for the fallen angels). If you look at the original texts of the Old Testament and the New Testament in the Ancient Greek, you will see that the first Christians did not worry about Hell because Hell did not exist for mortals. The idea of Hell for mortals came as pagan beliefs were incorporated into Christian doctrines and as late Roman Church leaders, who restricted access to the Bible to the elites and the priesthood, decided to use the threat of Hell and Damnation as a motivation to increase conversion to Christianity (and to gain wealth and political power). The Medieval and Modern Church simply followed the lead of the late Roman Church because they found it was easier to promote conversion (and to gain wealth and political power) as long as they threatened people with Hell and Damnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the unrequested history class that I already knew and that has nothing to do with my point<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059642#post1059642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erebus is a wonderful resource for the Garou. If they feel that they have committed a sin, they can subject themselves to the silver of Erebus in order to cleanse the taint from their souls and to gain forgiveness. On a more personal level, what mortal would not desire a place like Erebus, where they could find true cleansing and true forgiveness through their suffering while they are alive and could return to the world of living? I would not hesitate for a second to enter Erebus if I was guaranteed the cleansing and the forgiveness that the Garou receive from their suffering (and the guarantee that I would return to the world of the living).</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, you are talking EXACTLY like a religious fanatical. So, I wont discuss it further with you because it would be futile.<br /> And no, no SANE person wants to be brutally tortured in order to have its guilty and pain brainwashed away.<br /> Besides, if you believe in ANY of the bullshit you're talking, its very easy, just adopt the barbaric practices of medieval monks and inflict self torture, whip yourself in order to &quot;purify&quot;, its easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:02:05-08:00","id":1059652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059644#post1059644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I even find a hell of a fun to play with Red Talons (my favorite tribe), they just wanna rip humans off, and thats it.<br /> <br /> And... They ALSO dont think they are villains or monsters.<br /> <br /> And thats how ALL the Gaian theocracy should be seem BY THE PLAYERS.<br /> <br /> As an evil death cult.<br /> <br /> You know, real life terrorists also think they are blessed heroes doing the will of god or fighting for a better world.<br /> <br /> Thats how I see werewolves, as fanatics on a evil death cult, and that to me is OK.<br /> <br /> I dont see why thats a problemas, but I think its disturbing to see people that admire this kind of insanity (no, killing people is NEVER a good thing)</div> </div> </div> 