>Yes, while Werewolves can be defined as any way that the ST wants in Changing the Dreaming, Kindred of the East, Mage the Ascension, Vampire the Masquerade, etc, they are right according to the Werewolf the Apocalypse books. While the Garou have made mistakes in the past, are making mistakes in the present, and will make mistakes in the future, they are fighting on the right side and are fighting for all of the right reasons according to the books. While killing may not be good, it is right and it is justified, at least according to the books of Werewolf the Apocalypse, which is why they are epic heroes rather than inhuman monsters (or, if you want to think of them as inhuman monsters, they are in the same vein as Hellboy from the BPRD or the X-Men from the Marvel Universe).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:22:25-08:00","id":1059661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059652#post1059652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> problem is, their defined by the books as right.</div> </div> </div> </div>And so are the islamic Jihadists or christian Inquisitors.<br /> <br /> Just because its in a book does it make it right?<br /> <br /> Like 11twiggins said, thats akin to propaganda. &quot;Look, you dont have to worry about those details. What I tell you is right because Im telling you it is right&quot;.<br /> <br /> And again, its not a problem that the FICTIONAL Garou think that its ok to slice anyone in their way... Hell, I think the books should even stop all their BS and start putting the Garou and other Fera wanting nothing short than GENOCIDE for humans.... I would definetly play a game with Red Talons planning to commit HUGE onslaughts. I would play a Ratkin unleashing Ebola on New York.<br /> <br /> The problem for me is to see <u>real world players</u> saying out loud things that you would expect from a true psychopath like <i>pain is a tool</i>. That to me, is personally disturbing.<br /> <br /> It would be as if VtM players started saying that &quot;sabbat's practices are cool. Its fine and its GOOD to see humans like cattle&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:22:37-08:00","id":1059662,"title":"","content":"I prefer Shower misogi to cleanse myself, thank you very much.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://foxofinari.com/2016/06/29/solitary-shinto/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://foxofinari.com/2016/06/29/solitary-shinto/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://foxofinari.com/2016/06/29/solitary-shinto/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://foxofinari.com/2016/06/29/solitary-shinto/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T14:23:22-08:00","id":1059749,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Hey, folks. AgentSmith was a dummy account for the recently banned user, Karlgust. Accordingly, the new account has likewise been permanently banned.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:19:52-08:00","id":1059780,"title":"","content":"Our debate cut short, though I suppose it was getting circular.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:34:08-08:00","id":1059789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059571#post1059571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But here is the thing, is it immoral to destroy the oil refinery if it is creating poisons that turn innocent workers and innocent customers into Fomori? I mean, I feel for the 10,000 people whose community is ruined by the closing of the refinery, but their suffering pales in comparison to the 10,000 people per year that the products of the refinery will turn into Fomori, some of whom will be members of that community. The Garou do not fight against humanity, they fight against the Wyrm for all life (including humanity), it is just that humans are willing to accept a world that promotes the Wyrm without many questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMy problem with Garou morality is this (I mentioned this earlier in another post): The imperative to battle the Wyrm is a part of their religious fanaticism, and fails to take into account all variables. Now I know that the above example is just pulling random numbers out of the air, but let's actually look at it for a second. The 10,000 fomori per year is not supported by the text. It's explicitly stated that 99% of what Pentex does is in fact above-board (the other 1% being the <i>really</i> worrisome stuff). Much of what Pentex does is just camouflage for that other 1% as well as a huge cash cow. The stuff that it pumps out for general consumption inflicts low-level taint that is intended to destroy the world in the long term through aggregate. Moreover, they try to damage the environment as much as they reasonably can without tipping their hand to the otherwise generally clueless humans -- while also encouraging their &quot;competitors&quot; to follow suit in order to keep <i>their</i> profit margins competitive.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn the other hand, if the Garou manage to take down a major refinery or factory, the 10,000 innocent people out of work is probably entirely reasonable (especially if you figure in the knock-on effects if the closure occurs in a single-industry town). Now, if the Garou were to focus their efforts on just dealing with the 1% of Pentex that's crafting combat fomori, or concocting the next Thalidomide (TM), or whatever... that still leaves open a lot of moral issues. However if they monkeywrench a factory that's simply part of the money-making part of the ledger or is involved in the production of the King Beer that makes high school jocks just a<i> touch </i>more likely to do a date rape -- what exactly is the cost-benefit ratio if the entire town is out of work five years down the road and instead of drinking faintly Wyrm-tainted beer, they're drinking themselves to death and/or shooting heroin?<br /> <br /> \u200bI mention this only because that's (more or less) what's happening right now in the Rust Belt -- in the REAL WORLD. Donald Trump just got elected on <i>exactly</i> this issue (well, and the racism too, I suppose).<br /> <br /> \u200bBack in the World of Darkness, though, which serves the Wyrm more? 10,000 people lightly Wyrm-tainted, and faintly more awful than they would be normally, or the massive suffering, helplessness, hopelessness, frustration, anger (say directed at convenient scapegoats like Mexican immigrants or Muslims), suicide, and rampant substance abuse of exactly the same group?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 03-07-2017, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:50:45-08:00","id":1059798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059749#post1059749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:red\">Hey, folks. AgentSmith was a dummy account for the recently banned user, Karlgust. Accordingly, the new account has likewise been permanently banned.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Same IP Address? I'm curious to find out how this sort of thing is detected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T16:36:04-08:00","id":1059825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059798#post1059798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same IP Address? I'm curious to find out how this sort of thing is detected.</div> </div> </div> </div>IP address is usually the smoking gun. Sometimes people will sign up with the same email address. Suspicious-looking email addresses and familiar posting habits are common tip-offs, especially on accounts with small post counts. If a new user is posting like they've got a bone to pick with a regular or regulars, or engaging in a lot of aggressive posting with little regard for the rules, that's usually a red flag for sock puppetry, so when we notice them we investigate further to confirm or deny suspicions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-07-2017, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T17:43:37-08:00","id":1059847,"title":"","content":"OOps. very sorry","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":".  Post deleted with apolagies to mods 03-07-2017, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T18:54:24-08:00","id":1059872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1059493#post1059493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> So yes, &quot;Dave is too Wyld-obsessed&quot; is a totally fair reason (RAW) for his pack to drag him to Erebus and throw him in. And that could lead to decades of psychological torture as his beliefs which emphasize the Wyld over the rest of the Triat and Gaia (his deep-held religious beliefs) are presumably washed away. If only we had a word for washing away someone's psychological convictions using artificial methods...</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that Erebus isn't about how the Garou react to the Triat, but how the Triat reacts toward the Garou. It's about pattern spiders crawling inside their brain. The Wyld is fairly rare situation, but all members of the Triat are NOT your friend.<br /> <br /> It's the spiritual equivalent of Chemo therapy.<br /> <br /> And yes, the character is going to come out changed.<br /> <br /> If the character lovingly embraced the triat directly, then yeah. It's just hell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T05:21:16-08:00","id":1060029,"title":"","content":"Actually I'm a bit curious how come Erebus is presented so casually. I've always thought that even getting there was a problem, let alone surviving the ordeal and coming back to the world. It's the stuff of legends, not a washing machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T05:29:37-08:00","id":1060031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1060029#post1060029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I'm a bit curious how come Erebus is presented so casually. I've always thought that even getting there was a problem, let alone surviving the ordeal and coming back to the world. It's the stuff of legends, not a washing machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>So is that Illuminati-esk multinational umbrella corporation Pentex but every pup and their mother seem to know all about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T05:51:16-08:00","id":1060037,"title":"","content":"Erebus in W20 is as easy to find as any other Near Umbra Realm, the problem is convincing Cerberus to let you into it if you are not sufficiently Tainted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T05:56:01-08:00","id":1060039,"title":"","content":"About the whole &quot;Erebus it's torture &amp; brainwash&quot; sub-thread.<br /> <br /> Castigate, in Wraith, it's a thing. It hurts, but it defeats being eaten by the Shadow. And I see no one saying that they're inhuman fascist monsters for doing this particular thing.<br /> <br /> To put it otherwise: I take that &quot;anti Erebus&quot; people would refusse to go to the doctor to cure a terminal illness if anesthesics weren't invented? . Because, you know, medicine used to hurt a lot when my grandparents were young, and still was better than being ill...Why do people think that Taint, in a level worthy of Erebus, should be less real or less damaging than a medical condition?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T07:49:03-08:00","id":1060078,"title":"","content":"probaly because opinions and beliefs, also get amputated","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T08:35:03-08:00","id":1060105,"title":"","content":"Same with Castigate, as the Shadow does influence opinions and beliefs. Still, these foraneous opinions and beliefs are better gone, as any Wraith would attest .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T09:32:20-08:00","id":1060134,"title":"","content":"I don't think the beliefs and the like get cut off. I see Erebus as extreme therapy with visions of your actions and the effects of your actions. Being dipped in molten silver and having the mistakes of your life and the consequences of your actions flash before your eyes will change your viewpoint....eventually. I see it something like this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Everywhere your body touches silver, you burn. You tread trying to keep your head above the surface. Your claws attempt to find purchase on the shore, but the molten silver makes the rock slick. You loose your grip and slide beneath the surface.<br /> <br /> <i>You are back in your old childhood room. You are in your small twin bed with your lover. Your fellow cub. All senses, taste, smell, touch are of her. </i><br /> <br /> You struggle to breathe. You open your mouth to scream. Silver pours down your throat and sears your lungs.<br /> <br /> <i>You walk the sept with the blessing of Falcon upon you. Your mother wishes you to attend the trial. Guilt keeps you away at first. Fear of discovery forces you to the trial. Your lover stands in a circle of Elders, a metis pup in her arms. The Elders words blow past you meaningless. You stare at the girl, still a cub. Her own rite of passage delayed until the trail's end. You pray to Gaia she doesn't speak your name. She says nothing. She does not even look at you.</i><br /> <br /> There are moments of relief where you break surface. Air, not silver touches your burned skin. Then a wave crashes over you. You are drawn into the depths again.<br /> <br /> <i>You stare down at the body of your lover. Dead, killed by the Black Spiral Dancers. The pup mourns his mother's death, but all you feel is relief. You hear the elders whisper about the orphan's cub's future. The old shame returns and for a moment you consider speaking. &quot;This is my son, I will care for him.&quot; you consider saying. Then a Galliard comes and begs you to allow him to sing of your battle prowess at the moot. You turn away from the elders and the pup and follow the Galliard to Glory. </i><br /> <br /> You awaken and find yourself clinging to a rock. The silver waves lap at your feet. The tide rises and soon you will burn again.<br /> <br /> <i>A Child of Gaia pack wishes to join your sept. You are down warriors and have no reason to turn them away. Except the metis, a pup no longer, is with them. You had not thought about the metis pup in years. As your homid and whole children make pleasantries, you stare at the metis. His misshapen body conceals any resemblance to you. To your surprise, he stares back defiantly. He knows who I am, you realize. Suddenly, the secrets you thought safe in your lover's death is not so safe anymore. </i><br /> <br /> You cough up silver and blood. You gasp for air. You find a pattern to this madness. You break surface when you are about to suffocate. You barely get enough air to survive before being pulled back down again.<br /> <br /> <i>Arranging the metis' death was easy. Tragedy stalks the Garou at each step. You simply make a rare tactical error. Send the Child of Gaia pack into death. The Bawn will be cleansed of taint. When news of the pack's death came back to you, you thought you could rest easy. The simple mistake made in youth has been erased. Your position as Sept Alpha was safe. Yet when you sought your bed, whispers of death and decay haunted your dreams. Tempted you to more power. </i><br /> <br /> With your rare breath, you beg for mercy. You did what you did to protect your children. Sacrifice one misshapen pup for the rest. Yet more memories flashed. The hunger for power. The fall of your sept. The dance for even more power. Your children chanting the Rite of the Silver Forge.<br /> <br /> If it wasn't for him, you would not have been tempted. You would not have fallen.... Your crime was you should have killed him sooner.<br /> <br /> The silver is silent and without mercy. It chokes out your excuses and drags you back down again.<br /> <br /> <br /> ((It will be interesting to see what everyone thinks the Silver Fang's true Crimes are. ))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 03-08-2017, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T10:09:48-08:00","id":1060154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1060039#post1060039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To put it otherwise: I take that &quot;anti Erebus&quot; people would refusse to go to the doctor to cure a terminal illness if anesthesics weren't invented? . Because, you know, medicine used to hurt a lot when my grandparents were young, and still was better than being ill...Why do people think that Taint, in a level worthy of Erebus, should be less real or less damaging than a medical condition?.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between a surgeon cutting your leg off with a saw and a running it through a meat grinder. It's not pain I object to. It's torture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T10:33:19-08:00","id":1060162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1060037#post1060037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erebus in W20 is as easy to find as any other Near Umbra Realm, the problem is convincing Cerberus to let you into it if you are not sufficiently Tainted.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's always been easy to get to. Just that no sane, and very very few insanse, Garou wants to go there. It's a measure of last resort, for being touched by a member of the Triat that a simple Rite of Cleansing can't fix anymore. It's for those that are oozing green puss that kills plants on contact from a permanent wound, has pattern spiders crawling off their 'gift' armor strengthening the gauntlet around them, or is causing kudzu like growth of any moss in his path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T10:38:42-08:00","id":1060167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1060154#post1060154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a difference between a surgeon cutting your leg off with a saw and a running it through a meat grinder. It's not pain I object to. It's torture.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of pain = healing is as old as medicine itself. I am not sure if you are rejecting the idea of Erebus because it is too harsh in degree or because you think it should be spiritually unnecessary, but both seem to be misconceptions if we are reading the same books (not being smarmy, lots of my stuff is outdated).<br /> <br /> Werewolves are not squeamish about pain. Their rage drives them into situations where injury and agony are unavoidable. Physical suffering is a constant of life in the Garou Nation. Erebus is merely an extreme extension of what the Garou already know. Werewolves do not shy away from violence, they respond to it, react to it. If a Garou is in Erebus, there are not there to suffer mindlessly. The injuries they suffer force them to confront their own shortcomings. Spiritual corruption is real and deadly in WtA. Erebus is brutal and unpleasant, but it does serve a purpose. Hell, to use your example, perhaps running around in a meatgrinder may in fact be beneficial- a crazed, Wyld-tainted werewolf is getting their mutating in-flux body shredded over and over again. When all the warped flesh is carved off the Garou can regain a measure of sanity, and only when he regenerates his wounds without manifesting any mutations will he be free of the taint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 03-08-2017, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T10:54:32-08:00","id":1060176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1060134#post1060134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the beliefs and the like get cut off. I see Erebus as extreme therapy with visions of your actions and the effects of your actions. Being dipped in molten silver and having the mistakes of your life and the consequences of your actions flash before your eyes will change your viewpoint....eventually. I see it something like this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Everywhere your body touches silver, you burn. You tread trying to keep your head above the surface. Your claws attempt to find purchase on the shore, but the molten silver makes the rock slick. You loose your grip and slide beneath the surface.<br /> <br /> <i>You are back in your old childhood room. You are in your small twin bed with your lover. Your fellow cub. All senses, taste, smell, touch are of her. </i><br /> <br /> You struggle to breathe. You open your mouth to scream. Silver pours down your throat and sears your lungs.<br /> <br /> <i>You walk the sept with the blessing of Falcon upon you. Your mother wishes you to attend the trial. Guilt keeps you away at first. Fear of discovery forces you to the trial. Your lover stands in a circle of Elders, a metis pup in her arms. The Elders words blow past you meaningless. You stare at the girl, still a cub. Her own rite of passage delayed until the trail's end. You pray to Gaia she doesn't speak your name. She says nothing. She does not even look at you.</i><br /> <br /> There are moments of relief where you break surface. Air, not silver touches your burned skin. Then a wave crashes over you. You are drawn into the depths again.<br /> <br /> <i>You stare down at the body of your lover. Dead, killed by the Black Spiral Dancers. The pup mourns his mother's death, but all you feel is relief. You hear the elders whisper about the orphan's cub's future. The old shame returns and for a moment you consider speaking. &quot;This is my son, I will care for him.&quot; you consider saying. Then a Galliard comes and begs you to allow him to sing of your battle prowess at the moot. You turn away from the elders and the pup and follow the Galliard to Glory. </i><br /> <br /> You awaken and find yourself clinging to a rock. The silver waves lap at your feet. The tide rises and soon you will burn again.<br /> <br /> <i>A Child of Gaia pack wishes to join your sept. You are down warriors and have no reason to turn them away. Except the metis, a pup no longer, is with them. You had not thought about the metis pup in years. As your homid and whole children make pleasantries, you stare at the metis. His misshapen body conceals any resemblance to you. To your surprise, he stares back defiantly. He knows who I am, you realize. Suddenly, the secrets you thought safe in your lover's death is not so safe anymore. </i><br /> <br /> You cough up silver and blood. You gasp for air. You find a pattern to this madness. You break surface when you are about to suffocate. You barely get enough air to survive before being pulled back down again.<br /> <br /> <i>Arranging the metis' death was easy. Tragedy stalks the Garou at each step. You simply make a rare tactical error. Send the Child of Gaia pack into death. The Bawn will be cleansed of taint. When news of the pack's death came back to you, you thought you could rest easy. The simple mistake made in youth has been erased. Your position as Sept Alpha was safe. Yet when you sought your bed, whispers of death and decay haunted your dreams. Tempted you to more power. </i><br /> <br /> With your rare breath, you beg for mercy. You did what you did to protect your children. Sacrifice one misshapen pup for the rest. Yet more memories flashed. The hunger for power. The fall of your sept. The dance for even more power. Your children chanting the Rite of the Silver Forge.<br /> <br /> If it wasn't for him, you would not have been tempted. You would not have fallen.... Your crime was you should have killed him sooner.<br /> <br /> The silver is silent and without mercy. It chokes out your excuses and drags you back down again.<br /> <br /> <br /> ((It will be interesting to see what everyone thinks the Silver Fang's true Crimes are. ))</div> </div> </div> </div>This is almost exactly how my character's erebus trip went, nice! (Read it <a href=\"http://z6.invisionfree.com/Masquerade_Project/ar/t6169.htm\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, please note it was not the most uptightly played of games ^^'').<br /> <br /> So yes, this is good Revised era writing of the healing of Erebus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T11:47:21-08:00","id":1060197,"title":"","content":"Erebus exists to purify Garou of taint and sin (The Velvet Shadow, pp. 61-64). Taint could be considered to be the result of excessive exposure to one of the members of the Triat. Sin could be considered to be the result of actions that support a member of the Triat. In addition, beyond the physical purification by molten silver, the Harrowers and the Castigators work in pairs to purify the mind and soul of the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T06:17:28-08:00","id":1060490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1060167#post1060167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea of pain = healing is as old as medicine itself. I am not sure if you are rejecting the idea of Erebus because it is too harsh in degree or because you think it should be spiritually unnecessary, but both seem to be misconceptions if we are reading the same books (not being smarmy, lots of my stuff is outdated).</div> </div> </div> </div>I am rejecting the idea of Erebus because Torture is Of The Wyrm, and I don't mean the Dissolver, I mean the Corrupter Wyrm. I understand that the book says &quot;This is a place of healing&quot; and the only conclusion I can come to from that is &quot;That is clearly a BSD plot to trick people into going there&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T06:54:35-08:00","id":1060498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am rejecting the idea of Erebus because Torture is Of The Wyrm, and I don't mean the Dissolver, I mean the Corrupter Wyrm. I understand that the book says &quot;This is a place of healing&quot; and the only conclusion I can come to from that is &quot;That is clearly a BSD plot to trick people into going there&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a subtle, but relevant, difference between torture and an ordeal. Torture it's meant to break you, to make you do things you don't want to. An ordeal it's meant to be endured, it's a test. If Erebus it's a place of torture, it isn't very good at it's job, as it's unable to change you if you won't regret your actions in the first place (proved by the BSD that spend millenia there). If it's a place of punish, then it's quite forgiving, you can get out if you're sorry (not all versions of Hell give you a second chance). If it's an ordeal...yes, it's a very fearsome ordeal, it tests you with horrible pain, and if you fail you get to suffer forever.<br /> <br /> And what's more important, it works. Taint on a level that's beyond magical healing and sin goes away. If you're a walking wyrm fueled cancerous tumor in constant pain that wants to rape everything in sight, but have earned a moment of clarity and regret, you may want to go there to burn your misery away. Sure, it's scary, but it may beat the alternative.<br /> <br /> Werewolf it's the stuff of might, of epicness, it makes sense for them to have a place where they can purify at the cost of immense suffering. If Erebus was a nice place of healing, going there and returning renewed wouldn't be so <i>badass</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-09-2017, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T07:24:36-08:00","id":1060509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1060498#post1060498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a subtle, but relevant, difference between torture and an ordeal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. You're allowed to kill yourself to end an ordeal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1060498#post1060498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">proved by the BSD that spend millenia there</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for this. You've solved the conundrum for me. When it's time for The Apocalypse, the BSDs go to Erebus, drain the river, and an army of thousands of insane Garou that are immune to pain are there waiting for them, courtesy of the Garou Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T08:12:48-08:00","id":1060519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. You're allowed to kill yourself to end an ordeal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't aware that there was such a strict rule for somerthing to be called an ordeal...<br /> <br /> I thought that an ordeal was just:<br /> <br /> 1. any extremely severe or trying test, experience, or trial.<br /> <br /> 2. a primitive form of trial to determine guilt or innocence by subjecting the accused person to fire, poison, or other serious danger, the result being regarded as a divine or preternatural judgment.<br /> <br /> Nothing says that you're allowed to kill yourself...of course, usually you can, but then usually there aren't real pternatural forces actively working on you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thank you for this. You've solved the conundrum for me. When it's time for The Apocalypse, the BSDs go to Erebus, drain the river, and an army of thousands of insane Garou that are immune to pain are there waiting for them, courtesy of the Garou Nation. </div> </div> </div>Since Werewolf books were written by BSD anyway, maybe Apocalipse isn't so bad after all. Perhaps it's all a ruse to keep Garou fighting the Wyrm, to weaken the Nation untill BSD arrive...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-09-2017, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T08:15:16-08:00","id":1060520,"title":"","content":"The silver river cannot be drained, and there are only a handful of BSD in Erebus (it is probably really difficult to carry a stuggling BSD to Erebus without accidentally killing them, especially since their allies will likely target you during the trip). I honestly do not see why people think that being purified by Erebus is so horrifying. I would think that most people who play WTA would embrace such a simple and straightforward way to purify oneself of sin and taint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T08:37:05-08:00","id":1060531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1060520#post1060520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The silver river cannot be drained, and there are only a handful of BSD in Erebus (it is probably really difficult to carry a stuggling BSD to Erebus without accidentally killing them, especially since their allies will likely target you during the trip). I honestly do not see why people think that being purified by Erebus is so horrifying. I would think that most people who play WTA would embrace such a simple and straightforward way to purify oneself of sin and taint.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were put there before the rest of the nation realized the Spiral was permanent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T08:37:55-08:00","id":1060532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The silver river cannot be drained, and there are only a handful of BSD in Erebus (it is probably really difficult to carry a stuggling BSD to Erebus without accidentally killing them, especially since their allies will likely target you during the trip)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what the BSD want you to believe...they also want you to believe they are corrupted werewolves, but nothing it's further to the truth. In truth, BSD it's a Blood Line of vampires that fool the Garou into fighting each other and the Wyrm. This it's because GArou were created by Lilith to fiight vampires, and while it's impossible to divert them entirely from this purpose, because Lilit power it's too much, the True BSD did the next best thing and cursed the Wyrm to smell like vampires so the Garou would turn their attention to the Umbra and igniting the war that would consume the Nation.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T09:22:58-08:00","id":1060546,"title":"","content":"Not according to the books and the Lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T09:48:53-08:00","id":1060553,"title":"","content":"Aleph already touched on this with their intentional absurdisms, but this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1060490#post1060490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am rejecting the idea of Erebus because Torture is Of The Wyrm, and I don't mean the Dissolver, I mean the Corrupter Wyrm. I understand that the book says &quot;This is a place of healing&quot; and the only conclusion I can come to from that is &quot;That is clearly a BSD plot to trick people into going there&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that make any sense? If you don't like what is in the books, that is fine, change it in your game. As written, Erebus =/= torture, but if you want to tell a story that features the realm in a negative light, go for it. However, you seem to be claiming that the authors of the umbra books broke the 3rd wall in order to include a plot that involves Black Spiral Dancers spreading propaganda via OOC knowledge about Charyss and her realm. <i>That </i>is absurd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 03-09-2017, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T09:57:34-08:00","id":1060556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1060532#post1060532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what the BSD want you to believe...they also want you to believe they are corrupted werewolves, but nothing it's further to the truth. In truth, BSD it's a Blood Line of vampires that fool the Garou into fighting each other and the Wyrm. This it's because GArou were created by Lilith to fiight vampires, and while it's impossible to divert them entirely from this purpose, because Lilit power it's too much, the True BSD did the next best thing and cursed the Wyrm to smell like vampires so the Garou would turn their attention to the Umbra and igniting the war that would consume the Nation.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just reading this gave me a headache <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously though, I 100% agree with the perspective or Ordeal vs Torture.<br /> <br /> I don't understand the views present in this thread that make Erebus out to be a bad thing. Pain in Werewolf has never been something to shy away from (and pain in and of itself isn't &quot;of the Wyrm&quot;/&quot;evil&quot;). When all is said and done and a Garou completes their time in the river, the memories of the time there specifically fade. So while the Garou who comes out might have a differing outlook from when they went it, it is generally a decidedly clearer outlook. I don't think the Realm fundamentally changes anyone, outside of burning the Wyrm (usually) taint away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 03-09-2017, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T12:07:07-08:00","id":1060593,"title":"","content":"With Erebus, if you end up there you usually are not healthy in mind or soul. But more important than that, as much as I'm glad my character lived through it, he deserved every agg level he was given. I heard a phrase used once about portraying redemption to characters who have done wrong. What of the voice of their victims? Those they hurt and damaged and killed? Are they going to be silenced?<br /> <br /> <br /> To me, Erebus is that voice. The retribution for all the harm they did and lives they took needlesly.<br /> <br /> These are not good or nice people, they have hurt others willingly. Whether Weaver tainted, Wyld or Wyrm, to get far enough to need a silver bath, you still hurt and killed others. Especially with BSDs, even if they regret their deeds, their victims don't need to forgive them. Most possibly don't, ever. And that is their right, even if through erebus' rivers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T12:49:07-08:00","id":1060611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1060593#post1060593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are not good or nice people, they have hurt others willingly. Whether Weaver tainted, Wyld or Wyrm, to get far enough to need a silver bath, you still hurt and killed others. Especially with BSDs, even if they regret their deeds, their victims don't need to forgive them. Most possibly don't, ever. And that is their right, even if through erebus' rivers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. If you have been so tainted by one of the Traits less extreme methods of cleansing won't work, your mind has been corrupted by the trait. You would have committed awful acts in the trait's name. A character sent to Erebus may be sympathetic, but these aren't good people. Your average werewolf should not be sent to Erebus for simply breaking the litany. Hell, I don't think they should be sent for breaking the litany multiple times. Erebus worthy crimes are crimes combined with irreversible taint. This should be serial killer/rapist, traitor to the Garou nation, a whole sept died because of their actions. Really bad &quot;this guy is a villain of the story&quot; shit.<br /> <br /> Erebus has a place in the setting and that place is the path of last resort. Yes, it is an ordeal. Some may call it torture, but Werewolf is a brutal game. Erebus should be only considered when Death is the other punishment option. Death would be easier and more sure method of retribution, but some Philodox thought this corrupted soul was worth saving. So into the silver lake they go. If they make it out, then that vindicates the Philodox's judgement. If they don't, well.... Erebus is a fitting punishment for their crimes.<br /> <br /> Note, these are my opinions and how I would use Erebus in a game. YMMV","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 03-09-2017, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T14:55:43-08:00","id":1060670,"title":"","content":"I generally think that Erebus should also be used voluntarily by Garou who have committed other sins beyond being tainted. The weight of innocent lives lost to the Wyrm can be great, and Erebus offers an option other than Harano. Regardless of your sins, you are forgiven when you leave Erebus, though I think every Garou only gets one ticket in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T14:59:31-08:00","id":1060674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1060670#post1060670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally think that Erebus should also be used voluntarily by Garou who have committed other sins beyond being tainted. The weight of innocent lives lost to the Wyrm can be great, and Erebus offers an option other than Harano. Regardless of your sins, you are forgiven when you leave Erebus, though I think every Garou only gets one ticket in.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Heck, if some Garou wants to seek out Erebus to cleanse what she considers the taint of her soul, more power to her. I just don't think the Garou as a whole should be trigger happy with the Rite of the Silver Forge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T16:40:58-08:00","id":1060694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1060674#post1060674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Heck, if some Garou wants to seek out Erebus to cleanse what she considers the taint of her soul, more power to her. I just don't think the Garou as a whole should be trigger happy with the Rite of the Silver Forge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to treat going Erebus as the &quot; nuclear option&quot; since it can derail a campaign pretty quick, especially if the infraction is bad but not &quot;lake of burning silver bad&quot;. I'll usually have some elder philodox give the player or pack some epic deed to perform (go slay this wyrm thing or find missing caren X) to atone for what they done did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T15:59:32-07:00","id":1343876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again#post1053873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do all this work as a ST. You provide visuals, minatures, dry erase boards, character folders, maps, background info , lend your own books etc.....and then 1-2 players decide to loot every little thing they can see for no reason , charge into every scenario in Crinos despite overwhelming odds , OOC yell and argue and talk over you , ask you follow up questions before your finished answering their initial question...goddamnit.....<br /> <br /> full disclosure, I probably smoked a pack of cigarettes in leui of jumping over the table and taking it to the streets</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;He doesn't scare me. He makes power character I drop an elephant on it. He makes bigger and meaner character I use heavier elephant. I got a lot of elephants - figuratively&quot;<br /> Tony &quot;Listen up you primitive screwheads&quot;<br /> <br /> To revive this topic (and get it back to the original question) some of my advices. <br /> <br /> 1. Get your own copy of &quot;Listen up you primitive screwheads&quot;. It's for Cyberpunk 2020but you will find there some advices how to deal with different types of problem players.<br /> 2. Let your players form a team without your interference. They usually know their style of play so they won't spoil your efforts (or destroy it completely as a one team). I got a player that nobody wants to play with. And I don't want to be his ST. Luckily he forgot that I love to run games so much that he could form a one man team \ud83d\ude0b.<br /> 3. Exploit their characters strenght against them. &quot;Big power means big responsibility&quot;. If they are capable of dealing with any type of enemy they will get the most difficult tasks. And a properly generated First Team could wipe an entire sept out. I found the team like that somewhere in the Internet. Or use powerful NPCs (like The General from 7th Generation). Their sept is in the woods? How about few platoons of USMCs making their training grounds there (like in &quot;Dog soldiers&quot;). Or a B1 bomber &quot;accidentaly&quot; dropping a bomb right into the heart of the caern. And if you like Vampire 5th edition you could use Firstlight unit. They know and actively hunt vampires. Why not werewolves?<br /> 4. Use player's weakness against them. I run a CP2020 story once. In CP characters can have their stats from 2 to 10 (plus about 50% for cybernetic upgrades but the more upgrades you have the more psychotic you become) and skills from 1 to 10. The player's characters have their stats 20+ with minimum Humanity damage. Their previous GM allow it because they have bionic not cybernetic upgrades. One of them was some kind of mafia Don and two others were soldiers, his bodyguards. I run a story about a Don's lieutenant who wants to blow him from his saddle. The bodyguards stated that this is a game during which you have to think and went to sleep commanding us to wake them up in case of combat and the Don asked for my (GM) advice because his character has Inteligence 10 and he, as a player, 5 at most (IMHO he overestimated himself). In the end the Don lost everything and those players haven't bother me since then. Another example: I run Rage Across Australia campaign for a multitribal pack that acted like a bunch of psychos. Somewhere during the game they stated that they want a more combat-oriented, heroic game. So I send them to Russia to face the Zmei and Baba Yaga. When their characters wandered across Siberia they saw Gregornous Deathwing. They decided to hide but Ahroun Get of Fenris (macho Viking type character, played by a girl and equipped with a Great Klaive that has been in his family since early Middle Ages, with a Wind Spirit so it could return to character's hand) activate his Klaive. The dragon started to turning circles around them sensing magic of the Fetish. Their Ragabash tried to persuade Get to turn off his weapon but without success. And, when Gregornous locate them Fenrir jumped and throw his sword hitting the monster. His oponent roared bringing calamity (of course there is a saving throw but based on Empathy; what kind of Fenris will find this talent useful). I decided that the Wind Spirit was affected and weapon didn't return to his owner's hand. And wounded dragon started to fly away with the blade in his guts. What did the player's said? That I am unfair and chose the worst option I could use as a calamity affect. And they haven't bother me either since then. <br /> 5. Listen carefully what your players say. They will give you weapons to stop them. Example: another CP2020 game. In the middle of a firerfight in a bar one of players declared that his character gets up and walks to the bathroom. I asked him three times if he's sure about it. And then I killed his character. I don't know if it was a plain stupidity or a masterpiece of acting as shellshocked but he didn't show again so I assume the former. <br /> <br /> And remember, the worst enemy is the one that you don't see (like P....x).<br /> <br /> Hope I was helpful","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 10-28-2019, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T11:28:23-07:00","id":1344231,"title":"","content":"It is unfortunate that you have to go trough this. You have a particualr playstyle and they also have one as well and those two playstyles do tend to not mesh well. On top of that it seems that certain players do not care that they are running rampant over other players good time as they can not seem to see that this is a cooprative game and everyone should be able to play the way they want to play.<br /> <br /> My only advice is to try and make them understand that while you respect that they want to kill an loot everything adn would be willing ot write in particular things to allow them to do so they can not turn every encounter into this style of play as it does mean that they are forcing others to play their style and their style only.<br /> <br /> Their is one player at every table that does not get to kick in the door kill everything and loot the corpses, and that is the ST. They must provide such entertainment to others so others should be respectfull that the ST is technically a player too and one that puts in a lot of time and effort into providign the players a good time free of charage. In turn the players should try to provide the ST with a good time by trying ot get to know the plot and NPCs the ST took time to create.<br /> <br /> If they do not understand then ask them to leave the game. If they are not willing ot help their friend have a good time in the game with them then they are not your friends, as it seems they don't care about you or your feelings and only care about what you can provide for them.<br /> <br /> If the group falls apart join a discord put out a call for players and play on line with players that will respect that we are all in this together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T12:01:15-07:00","id":1344234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1344231#post1344231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is unfortunate that you have to go trough this.</div> </div> </div> </div> I do not feel unfortunate. Au contraire it amuses me. And get me tons of funny stories to tell. Ok, I prefere my plots to be unveiled and resolved by the powers of mind, charisma and sometimes force but I am a &quot;sandbox style&quot; ST and if my players want to use the latter only that's their right. They only have to deal with the consequences. Some of them endure it and are still my players some of them not and find another GM, more of their tastes.<br /> <br /> Of course I've also met creative players. Once I run Warhammer campaign for a group of average age 11. Their characters ended one adventure in a prison, accused of murder and waiting for an execution. I don't know if you are familiar with magic in Warhammer but to cast a spell you need a material component which disapears after the spell is casted. One girl, playing a sorcerer's apprentice casted Light spell on bars (which in turn became a material component for this spell and started to shine) to help the group escape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 10-29-2019, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T12:07:34-07:00","id":1344235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1344234#post1344234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not feel unfortunate. Au contraire it amuses me. And get me tons of funny stories to tell. Ok, I prefere my plots to be unveiled and resolved by the powers of mind, charisma and sometimes force but I am a &quot;sandbox style&quot; ST and if my players want to use the latter only that's their right. They only have to deal with the consequences. Some of them endure it and are still my players some of them not and find another GM, more of their tastes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I was meaning that for the OP. I should have made that clear my bad.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T12:16:07-07:00","id":1344237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053873-problem-players-make-me-never-want-to-run-a-game-again?p=1344235#post1344235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry I was meaning that for the OP. I should have made that clear my bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have to be sorry. It's good to know that there's some compassion in human race \ud83d\ude1c.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T13:24:45-07:00","id":1344246,"title":"","content":"Well OP, it sounds like you may have some munchkin players, completely focused on power, killing and looting. A few possible solutions:<br /> <br /> 1) They didn't heal the dying SL<br /> <br /> Make a note that later they will come across a cool sparring session. The judge will heal the combatants at the end and mention how many lives the Mother's Touch helped him save over the years.<br /> <br /> 2) Attacked the Corax<br /> <br /> Like one of the previous suggestions say, give an ominous warning (&quot;interesting, fascinating, are you sure ?, you can certainly try&quot;). Then say &quot;The Corax has no idea what you plan to do. Normally I don't say anything because I fully want you to think through your moves. But you don't have a way of guessing I wouldn't handwave that detail, so its only fair I mention it. But from here on out, its all up to you&quot;. Use these ominous phrases to reinforce the understated &quot;bad idea&quot; when needed.<br /> <br /> 3) The tainted bones<br /> <br /> Mention that its too big to carry even in crinos. But they can with some effort take a few teeth, ribs and a few claws. If they are not careful and touch them, then you can seed nightmares, dangerous hallucinations and other signs of Wyrm corruption. This plot hook will escalate in a way that serves to imprint the importance of the Rite of Cleansing and to be paranoid around anything touched by the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> 4) The optimizer<br /> <br /> Tell him that, barring any vetos, he can purchase what he wants if he has the XP at character creation. But only if there is a story reason for them. No backstory, no Merit.<br /> <br /> Sure, he can have the dogs. But where do they come from ? How much did they cost ? Are they licensed, are they trained ? Won't neighbors be suspicious if they are constantly hurt from combat ? Won't the vet call an animals rights group to investigate ?<br /> <br /> Who sold him the sniper ? Is it legal ? Is he even allowed to carry one around? If not, how is he sneaking it into places? Either way, he needs to find a permit or locate a black market weapons dealer.<br /> <br /> If he is a tech wiz and in the military, when did he get time to setup a successful civilian company ? Did he embezzle military resources and had black market connections ? Was he dishonorably discharged at some point ? <br /> <br /> All of this will create interactions for later. <br /> <br /> Hope these help. Don't give up, its possible they are used to more combat heavy games and haven't grasped that is not the feel you are going for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-28-2019, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T14:25:22-07:00","id":1344257,"title":"","content":"Ok, to add something to your ideas:<br /> <br /> 1) If they are power gamers they propably barely notice the comment about saving lives with Mother's Touch. Plus was this Shadow Lord pure or tainted? Id tainted there's no need to heal him. If pure then SL will propably ignore character's actions (this particular SL was weak so he didn't deserve to live), most tribes will cheer them up (SLs aren't the most popular tribe) so the only negative things that can affect their characters come from Children of Gaia and maybe Stargazers tribes. Of course this SL could have family and friends. And leaving a dying Garou without help isn't the most honorable thing. <br /> <br /> 2) IMHO either those players were combat hungry or they let their instincts guide them. Combat hungry players usually don't get the suggestions (so next combat will be the same) and good roleplaying should be rewarded, sometimes at the expense of other players. During one of my campaigns Shadow Lord eliminated two other PCs, Get and Silver Fang. Do you think those players were mad? No. They created new characters, one of them even created Gaillard only to praise SL cleverness.<br /> <br /> I could only agree with third and fourth ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 10-29-2019, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}